{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WUy5jYw4Mbd5yddTWepFKF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '核心 reframe：从 ''principled 2-axis framework'' 转为 ''comprehensive\n2\t  empirical study of VLA token pruning across architectures and tasks''。 π0.5 cross-suite\n3\t  数据摧毁了两轴独立性假设——random k=0.9 在 Object=9% vs Goal=62.2%，同一 token-independent connector\n4\t  跨 suite 差异达 53pp。 E5 attention pruning 数据（X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2% vs L2norm=42.6%）证明\n5\t  ''entanglement'' 不是 connector 的固有属性，而是 importance metric 选择的 artifact。 CV scaling\n6\t  law 仅在 Object suite 内部成立（Spearman ρ=-1.0），跨 suite 后 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm\n7\t  > random），平均 |ρ|≈0.45。 VTR 确认为 SmolVLA-specific 方案（OpenVLA VTC-only 全部失败），且 M=96\n8\t  dip (p=0.034) 暗示训练不稳定。 Title 改为 ''A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies\n9\t  Across VLA Architectures''。 仍然 submit CoRL，因为 5 models × 4 suites × systematic comparison\n10\t  是 substantial empirical contribution。 Claims 缩减为：(1) pixel-shuffle entanglement\n11\t  是真实的架构属性（C2 survives），(2) importance metric 选择 > connector architecture（new empirical\n12\t  finding），(3) VTR 在 pixel-shuffle 上实现 near-lossless compression（C4 survives as case\n13\t  study）。\n14\t\n15\t  '\n16\timagined_experiments:\n17\t- name: 'Cross-Suite Expansion: π0.5 + X-VLA + OpenVLA + SmolVLA × 4 Suites'\n18\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n19\t  description: '将所有 5 models 的 pruning 实验从 Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。 核心目的：验证 2-axis\n20\t    framework 的 cross-suite 一致性。 实际结果：framework 在 Object suite 上准确，但 cross-suite 后出现系统性偏差。\n21\t\n22\t    '\n23\t  expected_results:\n24\t    pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct: 9.3\n25\t    pi05_random_k09_goal_sr_pct: 62.2\n26\t    pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 54.0\n27\t    pi05_random_k09_long_sr_pct: 31.4\n28\t    pi05_random_k09_cross_suite_range_pp: 52.9\n29\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n30\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct: 89.6\n31\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 95.3\n32\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct: 80.0\n33\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_cross_suite_range_pp: 18.2\n34\t    xvla_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 97.6\n35\t    xvla_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct: 70.2\n36\t    xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 78.8\n37\t    xvla_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct: 27.5\n38\t    xvla_l2norm_k095_long_sr_pct: 47.0\n39\t    smolvla_k095_all_suites_sr_pct: <0.1 (all 4 suites)\n40\t    cv_strategy_spearman_object: -1.0\n41\t    cv_strategy_spearman_goal: -0.5\n42\t    cv_strategy_spearman_long: 0.5\n43\t    cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean: 0.45\n44\t    delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_object_pp: 36.0\n45\t    delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_goal_pp: 13.8\n46\t    delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_long_pp: -4.6\n47\t    delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_object_pp: 28.0\n48\t    delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_goal_pp: 8.5\n49\t    delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_long_pp: 17.0\n50\t    delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_object_pp: -1.8\n51\t    delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_goal_pp: 8.8\n52\t    framework_accuracy_pct: 62\n53\t    axis2_amplification_entangling_minus_independent_pp: 11.4\n54\t    e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_object_sr_pct: 99.2\n55\t    e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_goal_sr_pct: 98.2\n56\t    e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial_sr_pct: 88.8\n57\t    e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_long_sr_pct: 90.2\n58\t    e5_xvla_attn_mean_k05_long_sr_pct: 94.0\n59\t  result_rationale: 'π0.5 random k=0.9 在 Object 上出现 catastrophic cliff（9.3%），但在 Goal\n60\t    上仅下降至 62.2%——同一 linear projection connector、同一 random method、同一 k，仅 task distribution\n61\t    不同就产生 53pp 差异。这直接破坏 \"token-independent connector 不受 task complexity 影响\" 的核心假设。\n62\t    机制：Object suite 需要 precise object identity discrimination（visually similar condiments），random\n63\t    在 cliff zone 摧毁 concentrated discriminative features；Goal suite 的 task 由 language\n64\t    instruction 区分，vision tokens 冗余度更高，random 破坏的影响小。 L2norm 在相同 k=0.9 的 cross-suite\n65\t    range 仅 18.2pp（vs random 53pp），证明 cross-suite sensitivity 是 METHOD-dependent 而非\n66\t    connector-dependent。 E5 attention pruning 数据更具破坏性：X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2%（Object）、98.2%（Goal），vs\n67\t    L2norm=42.6%/59%。这意味着 X-VLA 的 \"entanglement\" 问题完全可以通过更换 importance metric 解决，BART\n68\t    encoder 产生的不是 \"irreversible entanglement\" 而是 \"norm-unfriendly importance distribution\"。\n69\t    CV scaling law 在 Object 内仍然成立（Spearman -1.0），但 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm >\n70\t    random，Δ=-4.6pp），导致 cross-suite 平均 |ρ|≈0.45，远低于 paper 声称的 \"universal predictor\"\n71\t    所需的 >0.8。 OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也出现 method preference reversal（random > L2norm +8.8pp），而\n72\t    Object 上 L2norm > random（+1.8pp）。同一 CV=0.215 的 model，跨 suite 后 method preference\n73\t    反转。 Framework 在 20 个 model×suite 预测中仅正确约 12 个（62%），达不到 \"principled framework\"\n74\t    标准。\n75\t\n76\t    '\n77\t  tables:\n78\t  - title: 'Table A: Cross-Suite Δ(Random-L2norm) at k=0.5 — CV Scaling Law Breakdown'\n79\t    columns:\n80\t    - Model\n81\t    - CV\n82\t    - Object Δ(pp)\n83\t    - Spatial Δ(pp)\n84\t    - Goal Δ(pp)\n85\t    - Long Δ(pp)\n86\t    - Range(pp)\n87\t    rows:\n88\t    - - π0.5\n89\t      - '0.055'\n90\t      - '+36.0'\n91\t      - '+16.0'\n92\t      - '+13.8'\n93\t      - '-4.6'\n94\t      - '40.6'\n95\t    - - X-VLA\n96\t      - '0.151'\n97\t      - '+28.0'\n98\t      - '+12.6'\n99\t      - '+8.5'\n100\t      - '+17.0'\n101\t      - '19.5'\n102\t    - - OpenVLA\n103\t      - '0.215'\n104\t      - '-1.8'\n105\t      - ~+5\n106\t      - '+8.8'\n107\t      - ~+3\n108\t      - ~10.6\n109\t    notes: Object suite 上 monotonic（ρ=-1.0），Long suite 上 π0.5 reversal 破坏 monotonicity。Cross-suite\n110\t      mean |ρ|≈0.45。\n111\t  - title: 'Table B: π0.5 Random k=0.9 Cross-Suite — Token-Independent ≠ Task-Independent'\n112\t    columns:\n113\t    - Suite\n114\t    - Baseline(%)\n115\t    - Random k=0.9(%)\n116\t    - Δ from baseline(pp)\n117\t    - L2norm k=0.9(%)\n118\t    - Method gap(pp)\n119\t    rows:\n120\t    - - Object\n121\t      - '98.2'\n122\t      - '9.3'\n123\t      - '-88.9'\n124\t      - '98.2'\n125\t      - '-88.9'\n126\t    - - Spatial\n127\t      - '97.2'\n128\t      - '54.0'\n129\t      - '-43.2'\n130\t      - '95.3'\n131\t      - '-41.3'\n132\t    - - Goal\n133\t      - '96.4'\n134\t      - '62.2'\n135\t      - '-34.2'\n136\t      - '89.6'\n137\t      - '-27.4'\n138\t    - - Long\n139\t      - '92.8'\n140\t      - '31.4'\n141\t      - '-61.4'\n142\t      - '80.0'\n143\t      - '-12.8'\n144\t    notes: Cross-suite range 53pp for random vs 18pp for L2norm。Task sensitivity 是\n145\t      method-specific，非 architecture-level property。\n146\t  - title: 'Table C: E5 Attention Pruning Demolishes Entanglement Narrative (X-VLA\n147\t      k=0.5)'\n148\t    columns:\n149\t    - Suite\n150\t    - L2norm(%)\n151\t    - Random(%)\n152\t    - Attn-Last(%)\n153\t    - Attn-Mean(%)\n154\t    - Best Attn vs L2norm(pp)\n155\t    rows:\n156\t    - - Object\n157\t      - '42.6'\n158\t      - '70.6'\n159\t      - '99.2'\n160\t      - '98.4'\n161\t      - '+56.6'\n162\t    - - Spatial\n163\t      - '58.8'\n164\t      - '71.4'\n165\t      - '88.8'\n166\t      - '91.6'\n167\t      - '+32.8'\n168\t    - - Goal\n169\t      - '59.0'\n170\t      - '67.2'\n171\t      - '98.2'\n172\t      - '97.4'\n173\t      - '+38.4'\n174\t    - - Long\n175\t      - '44.6'\n176\t      - '61.6'\n177\t      - '90.2'\n178\t      - '94.0'\n179\t      - '+49.4'\n180\t    notes: Attention pruning 在所有 4 suites 上实现 88-99% SR at k=0.5。问题不在 connector entanglement，在\n181\t      importance metric。\n182\t  figures_description:\n183\t  - 'Fig cross-suite heatmap: 5 models × 4 suites × 2 methods (L2norm/random) at k=0.5/k=0.9,\n184\t    颜色编码 SR。清晰展示 framework 预测（虚线框）vs 实际结果的 mismatch areas。'\n185\t  - 'Fig CV vs Δ(R-L2) scatter: 4 panels (one per suite), 每个 panel 3 个点 (π0.5/X-VLA/OpenVLA)，展示\n186\t    scaling law 在 Object 上线性但在 Long 上崩溃。'\n187\t  analysis: 'Cross-suite 数据系统性地破坏 2-axis framework 的两个核心预测： (1) Axis-1 独立性：token-independent\n188\t    connectors should be immune to task complexity → π0.5 random k=0.9 Object=9% vs\n189\t    Goal=62% 证伪（53pp gap）。 (2) CV universal predictor：CV 应在所有 suite 上预测 method preference\n190\t    → Long-horizon 上 π0.5 出现 reversal（L2norm > random），OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也 reversal。\n191\t    E5 attention pruning 数据进一步瓦解 Axis-1 定义：X-VLA（\"entangling\"）在 attention pruning\n192\t    下表现如同 \"independent\" connector。Axis-1 的区分不在 \"token coupling\" 而在 \"susceptibility\n193\t    to norm-based importance bias\"。 Reframe：论文不能声称发现了 governing principle，而应定位为 \"comprehensive\n194\t    empirical study revealing that importance metric selection matters more than connector\n195\t    architecture\"。\n196\t\n197\t    '\n198\t- name: π0.5 Token-Independent Confirmation (4B, Linear Proj)\n199\t  plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\n200\t  description: 'π0.5 作为 2nd token-independent data point，验证 CV=0.055 的 linear projection\n201\t    在所有 suite 上的 pruning 行为。 worst 档：π0.5 数据揭示 \"immune class\" 不存在——random pruning\n202\t    在 cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) 产生 catastrophic collapse，且行为极度 task-dependent。\n203\t\n204\t    '\n205\t  expected_results:\n206\t    pi05_cv: 0.055\n207\t    pi05_baseline_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n208\t    pi05_baseline_spatial_sr_pct: 97.2\n209\t    pi05_baseline_goal_sr_pct: 96.4\n210\t    pi05_baseline_long_sr_pct: 92.8\n211\t    pi05_random_k095_object_sr_pct: 71.1\n212\t    pi05_random_k0925_object_sr_pct: 27.6\n213\t    pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct: 10.8\n214\t    pi05_random_k085_object_sr_pct: 5.0\n215\t    pi05_random_k07_object_sr_pct: 75.5\n216\t    pi05_random_k05_object_sr_pct: 69.4\n217\t    pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n218\t    pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr_pct: 98.0\n219\t    pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr_pct: 33.4\n220\t    pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr_pct: 51.0\n221\t    pi05_random_cliff_depth_pp: 66.1\n222\t    pi05_l2norm_v_shape_depth_pp: 17.6\n223\t    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_cross_suite_avg_pp: 15.3\n224\t    pi05_attention_k07_object_sr_pct: 0.6\n225\t    pi05_attention_k05_object_sr_pct: 37.8\n226\t    pi05_attention_k095_object_sr_pct: 98.4\n227\t  result_rationale: 'π0.5（CV=0.055）本应是 \"immune\" class 的完美验证，但数据揭示了截然不同的图景： (1) Random-specific\n228\t    cliff：k=0.95→71.1% → k=0.925→27.6% → k=0.9→10.8% → k=0.85→5.0%，在 10% keep ratio\n229\t    变化范围内产生 66pp collapse。这个 cliff 是 random-specific 的——L2norm 在同区间保持 98.0-99.2% 的\n230\t    plateau。 (2) Fixed-mask experiment 排除了 temporal inconsistency（T0=12% = per-call\n231\t    12%），证明 cliff 是 spatial coverage 的 structural failure。 (3) V-shape non-monotonicity：L2norm\n232\t    在 k=0.5 出现 valley（33.4%），k=0.7=55.0% 和 k=0.3=51.0% 都更高。Token position visualization\n233\t    确认 k=0.5 恰好是 spatial clustering 最严重的点（1 cluster, 78% coverage）。 (4) Cross-suite\n234\t    数据摧毁 \"immune\" 标签：random k=0.9 在 Object=9% 但 Goal=62.2%（+53pp），Spatial=54%，Long=31.4%。Object\n235\t    的 concentrated critical features（visually similar condiments）在 cliff zone 极度脆弱，而\n236\t    Goal 的 language-disambiguated tasks 对 random token loss 更 robust。 (5) Attention\n237\t    pruning 不解决问题：k=0.7 attn=0.6%（比 random 的 75.5% 差 75pp），k=0.5 attn=37.8%（与 L2norm\n238\t    33.4% 持平）。π0.5 的 attention map 不提供有效 importance signal。 In worst tier, π0.5 从\n239\t    \"immune class exemplar\" 降级为 \"case study demonstrating that pruning behavior is\n240\t    an irreducible function of method × k × task, not a simple connector property\"。Cross-suite\n241\t    average Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5 = (+36+16+13.8-4.6)/4 = 15.3pp，远低于 Object-only 的 36pp。\n242\t\n243\t    '\n244\t  tables:\n245\t  - title: 'Table D: π0.5 Random Cliff Zone (Object Suite)'\n246\t    columns:\n247\t    - k\n248\t    - Tokens kept\n249\t    - Random SR(%)\n250\t    - L2norm SR(%)\n251\t    - Δ(L2-R)(pp)\n252\t    rows:\n253\t    - - '0.95'\n254\t      - '730'\n255\t      - '71.1'\n256\t      - '98.2'\n257\t      - '+27.1'\n258\t    - - '0.925'\n259\t      - '710'\n260\t      - '27.6'\n261\t      - '99.2'\n262\t      - '+71.6'\n263\t    - - '0.90'\n264\t      - '691'\n265\t      - '10.8'\n266\t      - '98.2'\n267\t      - '+87.4'\n268\t    - - '0.85'\n269\t      - '653'\n270\t      - '5.0'\n271\t      - '98.0'\n272\t      - '+93.0'\n273\t    - - '0.70'\n274\t      - '538'\n275\t      - '75.5'\n276\t      - '55.0'\n277\t      - '-20.5'\n278\t    - - '0.50'\n279\t      - '384'\n280\t      - '69.4'\n281\t      - '33.4'\n282\t      - '-36.0'\n283\t    - - '0.30'\n284\t      - '230'\n285\t      - '36.4'\n286\t      - '51.0'\n287\t      - '+14.6'\n288\t    notes: 方法偏好在 k=0.7 附近反转。Cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) L2norm 完胜；aggressive zone (k=0.5-0.7)\n289\t      random 完胜。\n290\t  - title: 'Table E: π0.5 Cross-Suite Random k=0.9 — ''Immune'' Class Falsified'\n291\t    columns:\n292\t    - Suite\n293\t    - Baseline(%)\n294\t    - Random k=0.9(%)\n295\t    - L2norm k=0.9(%)\n296\t    - Δ from baseline (random, pp)\n297\t    rows:\n298\t    - - Object\n299\t      - '98.2'\n300\t      - '9.3'\n301\t      - '98.2'\n302\t      - '-88.9'\n303\t    - - Spatial\n304\t      - '97.2'\n305\t      - '54.0'\n306\t      - '95.3'\n307\t      - '-43.2'\n308\t    - - Goal\n309\t      - '96.4'\n310\t      - '62.2'\n311\t      - '89.6'\n312\t      - '-34.2'\n313\t    - - Long\n314\t      - '92.8'\n315\t      - '31.4'\n316\t      - '80.0'\n317\t      - '-61.4'\n318\t    notes: 同一 model/method/k，cross-suite range=53pp。Framework 预测 token-independent\n319\t      应 <5pp variation。\n320\t  figures_description:\n321\t  - 'Fig π0.5 dual-method pruning curve: x=k, y=SR, two lines (random/L2norm), Object\n322\t    suite。突出 random cliff zone 和 L2norm V-shape valley。'\n323\t  - 'Fig π0.5 4-suite comparison: 4 panels, 每 panel 一个 suite, random+L2norm curves。展示\n324\t    cross-suite behavior divergence。'\n325\t  analysis: 'π0.5 数据是 worst 档的 smoking gun：CV=0.055 的 pure linear projection 不 \"immune\"，只是\n326\t    L2norm 恰好在 cliff zone 有效。 换用 random pruning，即出现 catastrophic cliff。换 suite（Goal/Long），random\n327\t    的 cliff 消失但 L2norm 的 advantage 也缩小。 这意味着 \"compressibility\" 不是 connector 的 intrinsic\n328\t    property，而是 (connector, method, k, task) 四元组的 emergent property。 2-axis framework\n329\t    的简化——将其压缩为 (connector, task) 二维——在 worst 档数据下失效。 Paper 需要 reframe：不是 \"connector\n330\t    determines compressibility\"，而是 \"we provide the first comprehensive map of the\n331\t    4D pruning landscape across VLA architectures\"。\n332\t\n333\t    '\n334\t- name: VTR Cross-Suite Generalization (SmolVLA M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\n335\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr\n336\t  description: 'SmolVLA VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long suites 上的压缩性能验证。 worst 档：VTR\n337\t    cross-suite recovery 衰减，且 VTR 训练在非 Object suite 上有不稳定性。\n338\t\n339\t    '\n340\t  expected_results:\n341\t    vtr_m32_object_sr_pct: 60.1\n342\t    vtr_m32_spatial_sr_pct: 53.2\n343\t    vtr_m32_goal_sr_pct: 56.4\n344\t    vtr_m32_long_sr_pct_predicted: 48.0\n345\t    smolvla_baseline_object_sr_pct: 59.2\n346\t    smolvla_baseline_spatial_sr_pct: 44.6\n347\t    smolvla_baseline_goal_sr_pct: 60.8\n348\t    smolvla_baseline_long_sr_pct: 36.6\n349\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_object: 1.015\n350\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial: 1.193\n351\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_goal: 0.928\n352\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_long_predicted: 0.874\n353\t    vtr_recovery_ratio_mean: 0.95\n354\t    vtr_m96_dip_p_value: 0.034\n355\t    vtr_m96_dip_confirmed: true\n356\t    hard_pruning_k05_all_suites_sr_pct: 0.0\n357\t  result_rationale: 'VTR M=32 在 Object 上实现 near-lossless compression（60.1% vs baseline\n358\t    59.2%），Spatial 上甚至超过 baseline（53.2% vs 44.6%，可能因为 VTR 训练 regularization 效应）。 但\n359\t    Goal suite recovery ratio = 56.4/60.8 = 0.928，低于 Object。预测 Long-horizon（未测）recovery\n360\t    ratio 进一步下降至 ~0.87：Long tasks 需要 multi-step reasoning，VTR 的 cross-attention 可能无法完全保留\n361\t    temporal action sequence 所需的 spatial information chain。 M=96 dip（p=0.034 vs M=64）在\n362\t    worst 档被确认为 training instability（非 statistical fluke），因为 M=96 的 3-seed std=3.2pp\n363\t    是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 VTR 的 flat M-curve 可能是 M=16-64 的幸运区间，M=96 暴露了 cross-attention\n364\t    query 数量与 pixel-shuffle token structure 之间的 resonance 问题。 VTR 仍然是 valid contribution（从\n365\t    0% hard pruning 恢复到 ~baseline），但 worst 档将其定位为 \"SmolVLA-specific case study\" 而非\n366\t    \"general method\"，因为： (1) cross-suite recovery 有衰减（Goal 0.93, Long predicted 0.87），\n367\t    (2) M=96 dip 暗示 training sensitivity， (3) OpenVLA VTR 完全失败（下条）。\n368\t\n369\t    '\n370\t  tables:\n371\t  - title: 'Table F: VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery (SmolVLA)'\n372\t    columns:\n373\t    - Suite\n374\t    - Hard Prune k=0.5(%)\n375\t    - VTR M=32(%)\n376\t    - Baseline(%)\n377\t    - Recovery Ratio\n378\t    rows:\n379\t    - - Object\n380\t      - '0.0'\n381\t      - '60.1'\n382\t      - '59.2'\n383\t      - '1.015'\n384\t    - - Spatial\n385\t      - '0.6'\n386\t      - '53.2'\n387\t      - '44.6'\n388\t      - '1.193'\n389\t    - - Goal\n390\t      - '0.0'\n391\t      - '56.4'\n392\t      - '60.8'\n393\t      - '0.928'\n394\t    - - Long (pred)\n395\t      - '0.0'\n396\t      - ~48\n397\t      - '36.6'\n398\t      - ~0.87\n399\t    notes: Recovery ratio 从 Object(1.0) 下降到 Long(0.87)。VTR 在 complex tasks 上 recovery\n400\t      衰减 ~13%。\n401\t  figures_description:\n402\t  - 'Fig VTR M-curve with error bars: x=M, y=SR, 3-seed error bars。M=96 dip 突出标注 p=0.034。'\n403\t  - 'Fig VTR cross-suite bar chart: 4 suites × (hard prune / VTR M=32 / baseline)，展示\n404\t    recovery gap 在 Long 上最大。'\n405\t  analysis: 'VTR 从 \"universal compression method\" 降级为 \"effective recovery tool for\n406\t    pixel-shuffle connectors, with decreasing efficacy on complex tasks\"。 M=96 dip\n407\t    的 statistical significance (p=0.034) 不足以证明 systematic failure（n=3 power ~0.2），但足以引起\n408\t    reviewer 对 training stability 的质疑。 Cross-suite recovery 衰减是合理的：VTR 在 Object suite\n409\t    上训练，cross-suite 是 zero-shot transfer。Long-horizon tasks 的 action sequence 依赖 precise\n410\t    temporal-spatial correspondence，VTR 的 cross-attention bottleneck 可能丢失这些 long-range\n411\t    dependencies。 Paper 策略：VTR 作为 §4.7 的 case study 保留，但移除 \"universal compression\"\n412\t    措辞，改为 \"recovers pixel-shuffle cliff-edge to near-baseline on trained distribution,\n413\t    with ~13% degradation on out-of-distribution complex tasks\"。\n414\t\n415\t    '\n416\t- name: 'VTR Universality Test: OpenVLA MLP Projector (M=128/32/64)'\n417\t  plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\n418\t  description: 'VTR 在 OpenVLA（MLP projector）上的泛化性测试。M=128 full VTR 已失败（0% SR），VTC-only\n419\t    M=32/M=64 作为 fallback。\n420\t\n421\t    '\n422\t  expected_results:\n423\t    openvla_vtr_m128_sr_pct: 0.0\n424\t    openvla_vtconly_m32_sr_pct_predicted: 3.0\n425\t    openvla_vtconly_m64_sr_pct_predicted: 5.0\n426\t    openvla_vtconly_m96_sr_pct_predicted: 2.0\n427\t    openvla_baseline_sr_pct: 74.0\n428\t    overfitting_confirmed: true\n429\t    failure_mode: model outputs identical action every timestep\n430\t  result_rationale: 'M=128 VTR 在 20K steps 后 0% SR（model 对所有 observation 输出相同 action）确认\n431\t    severe overfitting。 VTC-only M=32/M=64 预测同样失败（<5% SR），因为根本原因不在 VTR architecture\n432\t    而在 MLP projector tokens 的特性： (1) MLP projector tokens 已经是 individually meaningful\n433\t    的（CV=0.215, 有 gradient differentiation），VTR 的 cross-attention 无法提供额外信息，反而引入 information\n434\t    bottleneck。 (2) OpenVLA 的 256 tokens × 7B parameters 的 scale 与 SmolVLA 的 128 tokens\n435\t    × 450M parameters 完全不同——VTR 的 ~22M params 对 7B model 来说是 rounding error，无法学到有意义的\n436\t    re-encoding。 (3) M=96/M=64/M=32 的 training loss 持续下降但 eval SR 不恢复，典型的 action space\n437\t    overfitting pattern。 在 worst 档，这确认 VTR 是 pixel-shuffle-specific method。Paper 中\n438\t    VTR 需要 reframe：不是 \"universal compression tool\" 而是 \"architecture-specific recovery\n439\t    mechanism that works because pixel-shuffle tokens need re-entangling, while MLP\n440\t    tokens are already independent and don''t benefit from cross-attention re-encoding\"。\n441\t\n442\t    '\n443\t  tables:\n444\t  - title: 'Table G: VTR on OpenVLA — Universal Failure'\n445\t    columns:\n446\t    - Config\n447\t    - M\n448\t    - Params(M)\n449\t    - Steps\n450\t    - Train Loss\n451\t    - SR(%)\n452\t    rows:\n453\t    - - Full VTR\n454\t      - '128'\n455\t      - '22.2'\n456\t      - 20K\n457\t      - converged\n458\t      - '0.0'\n459\t    - - VTC-only\n460\t      - '32'\n461\t      - '22.2'\n462\t      - 100K\n463\t      - converged\n464\t      - ~3\n465\t    - - VTC-only\n466\t      - '64'\n467\t      - '22.2'\n468\t      - 100K\n469\t      - converged\n470\t      - ~5\n471\t    - - VTC-only\n472\t      - '96'\n473\t      - '22.2'\n474\t      - 100K\n475\t      - converged\n476\t      - ~2\n477\t    - - LoRA baseline\n478\t      - —\n479\t      - '883'\n480\t      - 100K\n481\t      - '0.065'\n482\t      - '0.0'\n483\t    notes: '所有 VTR configs 失败。Train loss 收敛但 SR ≈0。Failure mode: identical action\n484\t      output。'\n485\t  figures_description:\n486\t  - 'Fig overfitting diagnostic: training loss curve (converging) + eval SR curve\n487\t    (flat at 0%), 展示 train/eval disconnect。'\n488\t  analysis: 'VTR universality 完全失败。这不是 hyperparameter tuning 问题——M=128/96/64/32 全部\n489\t    <5% SR，且 LoRA fine-tuning 也产生 0% SR（libero_lora_baseline），说明 OpenVLA 的 fine-tuning\n490\t    本身就 fragile。 Reviewer 会问：\"如果 VTR 只在 SmolVLA 上 work，它是在修复 pixel-shuffle entanglement\n491\t    还是只是在 SmolVLA 的特定 action space 上 overfit？\" Response 策略：M=128 passthrough control（58.0%\n492\t    ≈ baseline 59.2%）证明 VTR 确实在学 re-encoding 而非 action space memorization。但这个 argument\n493\t    仅对 SmolVLA 成立。\n494\t\n495\t    '\n496\t- name: OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96)\n497\t  plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep\n498\t  description: 'OpenVLA 上的 VTC cross-attention compressor M-sweep。所有 M 值预期失败。\n499\t\n500\t    '\n501\t  expected_results:\n502\t    openvla_vtc_m32_sr_pct: 0.0\n503\t    openvla_vtc_m64_sr_pct: 0.0\n504\t    openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss: 2.45\n505\t    openvla_vtc_m96_sr_pct: 0.0\n506\t    all_m_values_fail: true\n507\t  result_rationale: 'M=96 已训完（final train loss 2.45, eval loss 2.66），远高于 SmolVLA VTR\n508\t    的 ~0.05 train loss。这不是欠拟合——100K steps with OpenVLA 的 tokenized action space 天然产生高\n509\t    cross-entropy loss。 M=32/M=64 的 v3/v4/v5 版本反复失败（disk full, GPU crash, training\n510\t    instability），即使成功训完也预期 0% SR。 根本原因：OpenVLA 使用 discrete tokenized actions（不是 continuous\n511\t    actions），VTC 的 cross-attention 将 256 个 vision tokens 压缩到 M 个 queries，但 OpenVLA\n512\t    的 LLM decoder 期望完整的 256-token vision context 来做 autoregressive action token generation。压缩后的\n513\t    M queries 无法提供 decoder 所需的 token-level spatial precision。\n514\t\n515\t    '\n516\t  tables: []\n517\t  figures_description: []\n518\t  analysis: '确认 VTR/VTC 在 MLP projector + discrete action space 的组合下无效。 Paper 中作为\n519\t    negative result 报告：VTR effectiveness = f(connector_type)，strengthens architecture-dependency\n520\t    narrative。\n521\t\n522\t    '\n523\t- name: X-VLA Cliff Threshold Localization (k=0.80/0.85, 3-seed)\n524\t  plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization\n525\t  description: 'X-VLA 在 k=0.80 和 k=0.85 的 3-seed 精确定位 cliff。Non-monotonic pattern\n526\t    已确认。 worst 档：cliff 是真实的，但 E5 attention pruning 证明它是 L2norm-specific artifact。\n527\t\n528\t    '\n529\t  expected_results:\n530\t    xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_mean: 89.0\n531\t    xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_std: 0.72\n532\t    xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_mean: 67.9\n533\t    xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_std: 0.31\n534\t    xvla_l2norm_nonmonotonic_gap_pp: 21.1\n535\t    xvla_random_k085_sr_mean: 63.6\n536\t    xvla_random_k080_sr_mean: 89.4\n537\t    xvla_e5_attn_k05_sr_mean: 98.4\n538\t    cliff_is_l2norm_specific: true\n539\t    cliff_is_method_independent: false\n540\t  result_rationale: 'X-VLA k=0.85 L2norm = 67.9%±0.31pp（3-seed，SD<1pp 确认完全 deterministic）。k=0.80\n541\t    = 89.0%±0.72pp。 Non-monotonic gap = 21.1pp（k=0.85 < k=0.80），2-token 差异产生 21pp\n542\t    SR change。Random pruning 在同区间也出现 cliff（63.6% vs 89.4%），但 per-task crash pattern\n543\t    不同（T4, T6 both crash across methods → architectural bottleneck）。 在 worst 档，这个\n544\t    cliff 的意义被 E5 attention pruning 完全重新诠释： - L2norm k=0.5 = 42.6% → attn_last k=0.5\n545\t    = 99.2%（+56.6pp） - 同样的 50 tokens，同样的 k=0.5（保留 25 tokens），attention 几乎完美而 L2norm\n546\t    catastrophic - 因此 cliff 不是 \"BART encoder entanglement creates irreversible token\n547\t    dependencies\"，而是 \"L2norm 在 BART encoder 的 near-uniform norm distribution 上退化为\n548\t    spatially clustered selection\" - Reviewer argument：\"如果换 importance metric 就消除了\n549\t    cliff，那 Axis-1 的 ''token coupling'' 定义有根本缺陷——关键不在 coupling 而在 importance metric。\"\n550\t\n551\t    '\n552\t  tables:\n553\t  - title: 'Table H: X-VLA Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic'\n554\t    columns:\n555\t    - k\n556\t    - L2norm SR(%)\n557\t    - L2norm SD(pp)\n558\t    - Random SR(%)\n559\t    - Attn-Last SR(%)\n560\t    rows:\n561\t    - - '0.90'\n562\t      - '97.6'\n563\t      - —\n564\t      - '97.8'\n565\t      - ~99\n566\t    - - '0.85'\n567\t      - '67.9'\n568\t      - '0.31'\n569\t      - '63.6'\n570\t      - ~97\n571\t    - - '0.80'\n572\t      - '89.0'\n573\t      - '0.72'\n574\t      - '89.4'\n575\t      - ~99\n576\t    - - '0.70'\n577\t      - '56.2'\n578\t      - —\n579\t      - '65.2'\n580\t      - '99.2'\n581\t    - - '0.50'\n582\t      - '42.6'\n583\t      - —\n584\t      - '70.6'\n585\t      - '99.2'\n586\t    notes: Attention pruning 完全消除 cliff 和 degradation。问题在 metric 不在 architecture。\n587\t  figures_description:\n588\t  - 'Fig X-VLA 3-method comparison: L2norm (cliff+degradation), Random (moderate degradation),\n589\t    Attention (near-flat). 三条 curve 在同一 plot 上，清晰展示 metric choice 的 decisive role。'\n590\t  analysis: 'Cliff localization 数据本身是 solid experimental result。但在 worst 档，E5 data\n591\t    完全改变其解读： cliff 不是 connector architecture 的 intrinsic property，而是 L2norm importance\n592\t    metric 在 low-CV distribution 上的 pathological behavior。 Attention pruning（zero\n593\t    additional training）消除所有 degradation，这意味着 BART encoder 并没有 \"entangle\" tokens in\n594\t    a way that prevents pruning，它只是让 tokens 的 L2-norm 不再是 good importance proxy。 Paper\n595\t    需要重新定义 Axis-1：从 \"token coupling\" 改为 \"importance metric suitability\"，或者承认 2-axis\n596\t    framework 是 L2norm-specific observation 而非 architecture-level insight。\n597\t\n598\t    '\n599\t- name: OFT CV Diagnostic (Token Importance Measurement)\n600\t  plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv\n601\t  description: 'OpenVLA-OFT 的 token importance CV 测量。Expected CV≈0.219（≈Standard OpenVLA）。\n602\t\n603\t    '\n604\t  expected_results:\n605\t    oft_cv: 0.219\n606\t    oft_cv_std: 0.012\n607\t    oft_entropy: 0.667\n608\t    openvla_standard_cv: 0.215\n609\t    cv_delta_pp: 0.4\n610\t    sr_eval_blocked: true\n611\t    gpu_incompatibility: Blackwell SDPA requires A100+torch2.2\n612\t  result_rationale: 'OFT CV=0.219 ≈ Standard OpenVLA CV=0.215（Δ=0.004），确认 connector（3-layer\n613\t    MLP）而非 action head（OFT vs standard）决定 token importance distribution。 Entropy 也几乎相同（0.667\n614\t    vs 0.661）。这是 framework 的 positive confirmation——same connector → same CV → same\n615\t    predicted pruning behavior。 但在 worst 档，这个 data point 的价值有限： (1) 无法在 LIBERO 上 eval\n616\t    SR（Blackwell GPU SDPA 不兼容），所以 CV 预测没有 ground truth 验证 (2) OFT 和 Standard OpenVLA\n617\t    用相同 connector 产生相同 CV 是 trivially expected，不提供 additional discrimination power\n618\t    (3) Reviewer 会指出：\"你们有 6 个 model 的 CV，但只有 4 个能实际 eval SR。CV 作为 predictor 的 validation\n619\t    set 太小。\"\n620\t\n621\t    '\n622\t  tables:\n623\t  - title: 'Table I: Diagnostic Metrics — 6-Model Spectrum'\n624\t    columns:\n625\t    - Model\n626\t    - Connector\n627\t    - CV\n628\t    - Entropy\n629\t    - Eval SR Available?\n630\t    rows:\n631\t    - - π0\n632\t      - Pure linear\n633\t      - '0.038'\n634\t      - '0.959'\n635\t      - Offline only\n636\t    - - π0.5\n637\t      - Pure linear (×√d)\n638\t      - '0.055'\n639\t      - —\n640\t      - Yes (4 suites)\n641\t    - - X-VLA\n642\t      - Linear + BART 12L\n643\t      - '0.151'\n644\t      - '0.614'\n645\t      - Yes (4 suites)\n646\t    - - OpenVLA\n647\t      - 3-layer MLP\n648\t      - '0.215'\n649\t      - '0.661'\n650\t      - Yes (Object only)\n651\t    - - OFT\n652\t      - 3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP)\n653\t      - '0.219'\n654\t      - '0.667'\n655\t      - No (GPU blocked)\n656\t    - - SmolVLA\n657\t      - Pixel-shuffle\n658\t      - '0.314'\n659\t      - '0.952'\n660\t      - Yes (4 suites)\n661\t    notes: 6 models 有 CV，但仅 3 models 有 full cross-suite SR。OFT 和 π0 只有 diagnostic\n662\t      metrics。\n663\t  figures_description: []\n664\t  analysis: 'OFT CV 完成了 6-model diagnostic table，但不改变任何结论。在 worst 档，这是 incrementally\n665\t    supportive 而非 decisive evidence。\n666\t\n667\t    '\n668\t- name: OFT Full Graded-Class Evaluation (4 Suites)\n669\t  plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full\n670\t  description: 'OpenVLA-OFT 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 上的 baseline + pruning evaluation。\n671\t    worst 档：GPU 不兼容问题持续，无法完成 evaluation。\n672\t\n673\t    '\n674\t  expected_results:\n675\t    eval_blocked: true\n676\t    blocker: Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility with OpenVLA-OFT\n677\t    workaround_attempted: A100 rental, torch2.2 downgrade — both failed\n678\t    fallback_evidence: CV=0.219≈OpenVLA, entropy=0.667≈0.661 — inferred graded behavior\n679\t    paper_impact: Missing 2nd graded-class SR data point, relies on CV inference\n680\t    reviewer_risk: Moderate — 2/3 connector classes have ≥2 SR-evaluated models, MLP\n681\t      class has only 1\n682\t  result_rationale: 'OFT evaluation 在 worst 档仍然被 GPU 不兼容阻塞。Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA implementation\n683\t    与 OFT checkpoint 的 torch 版本不兼容，降级 torch 或租用 A100 都不可行（timeline 限制）。 Paper 只能用\n684\t    CV/entropy comparison 间接 argue OFT follows OpenVLA pattern。Reviewer 会注意到 MLP projector\n685\t    class 只有 OpenVLA 1 个 model 有 SR data，不足以 generalize。 CogACT（literature baseline,\n686\t    MLP projector, 74.8%→74.2% under 78% pruning from EfficientVLA）可以作为 external evidence，但不是\n687\t    our own evaluation。 In worst tier, this is a clear gap but not fatal — pixel-shuffle\n688\t    (SmolVLA, 1 model, universal 0%) and linear (π0/π0.5, 2 models, variable) are\n689\t    well-characterized. MLP class has 1 internal + 1 external data point.\n690\t\n691\t    '\n692\t  tables: []\n693\t  figures_description: []\n694\t  analysis: 'Missing OFT SR data 在 worst 档是 acknowledged limitation。Reviewer concern\n695\t    等级 \"moderate\"——不会 reject paper，但会要求 camera-ready 补充或更 cautious language about\n696\t    MLP class generalization。\n697\t\n698\t    '\n699\t- name: Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo) — 3rd Connector Family\n700\t  plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\n701\t  description: 'RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) 在 LIBERO 上 fine-tune\n702\t    + pruning。 worst 档：fine-tuning 产生低 baseline，且 Perceiver 不清晰地落入 2-axis taxonomy。\n703\t\n704\t    '\n705\t  expected_results:\n706\t    fine_tuning_baseline_sr_pct_predicted: 18.0\n707\t    fine_tuning_difficulty: high — requires custom training pipeline adaptation\n708\t    perceiver_cv_predicted: 0.28\n709\t    perceiver_pruning_k09_predicted_sr_pct: 4.0\n710\t    perceiver_pruning_k05_predicted_sr_pct: 0.0\n711\t    taxonomy_fit: ambiguous — cross-attention creates partial entanglement different\n712\t      from both pixel-shuffle and BART\n713\t    paper_inclusion: dropped — insufficient time and unclear taxonomy value\n714\t  result_rationale: 'RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档面临多重困难： (1) Fine-tuning infrastructure：RoboFlamingo\n715\t    使用 Flamingo-style cross-attention perceiver resampler，将 variable-length vision\n716\t    tokens 压缩到 fixed 64 queries。这需要 custom training pipeline，previous attempts (train_c5_roboflamingo_v2)\n717\t    被 killed。 (2) Low baseline：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 在 LIBERO manipulation\n718\t    tasks 上可能不如 direct projection（SmolVLA 59.2%, OpenVLA 74%），因为 LIBERO 需要 precise\n719\t    spatial information 而 perceiver 天然是 lossy compression。预测 baseline ~18% SR。 (3)\n720\t    Taxonomy ambiguity：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 与 BART encoder 的 self-attention\n721\t    和 pixel-shuffle 的 spatial folding 都不同。它是 \"learned entanglement\" 而非 \"structural\n722\t    entanglement\"。CV 可能在 0.2-0.3 range，不清晰地落入现有 taxonomy。 (4) Timeline：距 abstract\n723\t    deadline 1 天，paper deadline 4 天，没有时间 debug fine-tuning pipeline + run full evaluation。\n724\t    In worst tier, RoboFlamingo 被 dropped from paper。这减少了 paper 的 connector family\n725\t    覆盖（3→2 confirmed families），但避免了 messy data 进一步复杂化已经 fragile 的 framework。\n726\t\n727\t    '\n728\t  tables: []\n729\t  figures_description: []\n730\t  analysis: 'Dropping RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档是 rational choice：paper 已经有足够的 models（5\n731\t    models × 4 suites）作为 empirical contribution，加入一个 low-baseline 的新 connector 只会模糊\n732\t    narrative。 但这意味着 paper 的 connector 覆盖限于 linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle 三类，reviewer 可能指出\n733\t    \"what about attention-based connectors (Perceiver, Q-Former)?\" 作为 limitation。\n734\t\n735\t    '\n736\t- name: VTR M-Sweep Completion (SmolVLA 3-seed × 5 M-values)\n737\t  plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\n738\t  description: 'SmolVLA VTR M-sweep 的 3-seed 完成和 MLP adapter control。 worst 档：数据 solid\n739\t    但 M=96 dip 和 high variance 引起质疑。\n740\t\n741\t    '\n742\t  expected_results:\n743\t    m16_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 56.9\n744\t    m16_3seed_std_pp: 1.3\n745\t    m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 60.1\n746\t    m32_3seed_std_pp: 1.3\n747\t    m64_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 62.0\n748\t    m64_3seed_std_pp: 2.3\n749\t    m96_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 54.5\n750\t    m96_3seed_std_pp: 3.2\n751\t    m128_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 58.0\n752\t    m128_3seed_std_pp: 3.5\n753\t    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 63.4\n754\t    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std_pp: 2.6\n755\t    vtc_vs_mlp_pvalue: 0.15\n756\t    m64_vs_m96_pvalue: 0.034\n757\t    baseline_sr_pct: 59.2\n758\t    m_curve_flat_within_3pp: true\n759\t    m96_dip_significant: true\n760\t  result_rationale: 'VTR M-sweep 数据 intrinsically solid：M=16(56.9%) 到 M=128(58.0%)\n761\t    都在 baseline 59.2% 的 ±5pp 内，证明 near-lossless compression at any ratio。MLP adapter\n762\t    control（63.4%）与 VTC（60.1%）无显著差异（p=0.15），确认 architecture independence。 但 worst\n763\t    档关注两个 weakness： (1) M=96 dip（54.5%, p=0.034 vs M=64=62.0%）虽然在 Bonferroni correction\n764\t    后 marginally significant，但 3.2pp std 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 training instability——某些\n765\t    seed/M 组合在 training dynamics 中进入 suboptimal basin。 (2) M=128 passthrough 的 3.5pp\n766\t    std 也高，且 seed43=54.0% 是 outlier（其他两个 seed 59.8/60.2%）。如果 passthrough control 本身有\n767\t    6pp variance，\"near-lossless\" 的声称需要 caveat。 In worst tier, VTR 仍然是 valid method（0%→~59%\n768\t    recovery），但 training stability concern 使其从 \"recommended practice\" 降级为 \"promising\n769\t    but needs further investigation\"。\n770\t\n771\t    '\n772\t  tables:\n773\t  - title: 'Table J: VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Results'\n774\t    columns:\n775\t    - M\n776\t    - Compression(%)\n777\t    - Mean SR(%)\n778\t    - Std(pp)\n779\t    - Individual Seeds\n780\t    - vs Baseline\n781\t    rows:\n782\t    - - '16'\n783\t      - '87.5'\n784\t      - '56.9'\n785\t      - '1.3'\n786\t      - 55.8/58.4/56.5\n787\t      - -2.3pp\n788\t    - - '32'\n789\t      - '75.0'\n790\t      - '60.1'\n791\t      - '1.3'\n792\t      - 61.6/59.2/59.6\n793\t      - +0.9pp\n794\t    - - '64'\n795\t      - '50.0'\n796\t      - '62.0'\n797\t      - '2.3'\n798\t      - 61.6/60.0/64.4\n799\t      - +2.8pp\n800\t    - - '96'\n801\t      - '25.0'\n802\t      - '54.5'\n803\t      - '3.2'\n804\t      - 52.6/58.2/52.8\n805\t      - -4.7pp\n806\t    - - '128'\n807\t      - '0.0'\n808\t      - '58.0'\n809\t      - '3.5'\n810\t      - 59.8/54.0/60.2\n811\t      - -1.2pp\n812\t    - - MLP-32\n813\t      - '75.0'\n814\t      - '63.4'\n815\t      - '2.6'\n816\t      - 65.2/64.6/60.4\n817\t      - +4.2pp\n818\t    notes: M=96 dip p=0.034。M=128 seed43=54.0 outlier。Flat M-curve 成立但 variance 在高\n819\t      M 处增大。\n820\t  figures_description:\n821\t  - Fig M-curve with 3-seed error bars and baseline band (59.2%±3pp shaded). M=96\n822\t    dip 和 M=128 variance clearly visible。\n823\t  analysis: 'VTR 在 worst 档仍是 paper 的 positive contribution：hard pruning 0% → VTR ~59%\n824\t    ≈ baseline 是 dramatic recovery。 但 M=96 dip 和 high-M variance 需要 honest reporting。建议\n825\t    paper 用 M=32 或 M=64 作为 recommended setting（stable seeds, good compression ratio），将\n826\t    M=96 dip 作为 \"open question: why does M=96 underperform?\" 放入 discussion。 Reviewer\n827\t    concern level: low-moderate. VTR 的 core claim（recovery from 0% to baseline）is\n828\t    robust. M=96 是 interesting anomaly 但不 undermine main contribution。\n829\t\n830\t    '\n831\t- name: Consolidated Cross-Suite Framework Accuracy Assessment\n832\t  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n833\t  description: '综合所有 cross-suite 数据的 framework 准确率评估。 worst 档：framework accuracy ~62%，不足以支撑\n834\t    \"principled framework\" 定位。\n835\t\n836\t    '\n837\t  expected_results:\n838\t    framework_predictions_total: 20\n839\t    framework_predictions_correct: 12\n840\t    framework_accuracy_pct: 62\n841\t    claims_surviving_review: 2.5\n842\t    surviving_claims: C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement), C4 (VTR case study), partial\n843\t      C3b (MLP graded)\n844\t    failed_claims: C1 (2-axis framework as principled theory), C5 (CV universal predictor)\n845\t    reframed_claims: C1→empirical observation catalog, C5→within-suite heuristic\n846\t    paper_contribution_type: empirical study with surprising findings\n847\t    corl_submission_viable: true\n848\t    corl_acceptance_probability_pct: 45\n849\t  result_rationale: 'Framework accuracy 计算方法： - SmolVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"catastrophic\n850\t    at k=0.95\" → 实际 all suites ≤0.1% → 4/4 correct - X-VLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"entangling,\n851\t    task-dependent collapse\" → Object OK (97.6%), Goal 70.2% (partial collapse), Spatial\n852\t    78.8% (moderate), Long 27.5% (collapse) → 3/4 correct（Object 不 collapse，与预测不符）\n853\t    - π0.5 × 4 suites: 预测 \"independent, immune to task complexity\" → Object random\n854\t    k=0.9=9%（NOT immune!），但 L2norm=98.2% → method-dependent → 1/4 correct（框架不区分 method）\n855\t    - OpenVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"graded, L2norm preferred\" → Object L2norm>random (+1.8pp\n856\t    ✓), Goal random>L2norm (+8.8pp ✗) → 2/4 correct - π0 × offline: 预测 \"immune\" →\n857\t    k=0.1 improves → 1/1 correct Total: 4+3+1+2+1 = 11/17 = 65%（≈62% with margin of\n858\t    error）\n859\t\n860\t    Claims survival analysis: - C1 (2-axis framework): FAILS as theory → survives\n861\t    as \"descriptive taxonomy for L2norm pruning on Object suite\" - C2 (pixel-shuffle\n862\t    entanglement): SURVIVES — universal 0% across all suites/methods/k is unambiguous\n863\t    - C3a (linear proj depends on pipeline): Partially survives — π0 immune, π0.5\n864\t    method-dependent, X-VLA cliff - C3b (MLP graded): Survives on Object — graded\n865\t    curve confirmed - C4 (VTR): Survives as SmolVLA case study — 0%→59% recovery -\n866\t    C5 (CV predicts strategy): FAILS as universal law → survives as \"within-Object-suite\n867\t    heuristic\"\n868\t\n869\t    2.5 claims survive: C2, C4, half of C3b.\n870\t\n871\t    CoRL viability: paper 作为 \"comprehensive empirical study\" 仍然 viable（5 models ×\n872\t    4 suites × 3 methods 是任何 VLA pruning 工作中最大规模的 comparison）。Acceptance probability\n873\t    ~45%——足够好的 empirical contribution 但缺少 unified theory 会让某些 reviewers 觉得 \"incremental\"。\n874\t\n875\t    '\n876\t  tables:\n877\t  - title: 'Table K: Framework Prediction Accuracy by Model'\n878\t    columns:\n879\t    - Model\n880\t    - Connector Class\n881\t    - Framework Prediction\n882\t    - Object\n883\t    - Spatial\n884\t    - Goal\n885\t    - Long\n886\t    - Accuracy\n887\t    rows:\n888\t    - - SmolVLA\n889\t      - Pixel-shuffle\n890\t      - Catastrophic all suites\n891\t      - ✓\n892\t      - ✓\n893\t      - ✓\n894\t      - ✓\n895\t      - 4/4\n896\t    - - X-VLA\n897\t      - BART encoder\n898\t      - Task-dependent collapse\n899\t      - ✗(no collapse)\n900\t      - ✓\n901\t      - ✓\n902\t      - ✓\n903\t      - 3/4\n904\t    - - π0.5\n905\t      - Linear proj\n906\t      - Immune to task complexity\n907\t      - ✗(random cliff)\n908\t      - ✗\n909\t      - ✗\n910\t      - ✗\n911\t      - 1/4\n912\t    - - OpenVLA\n913\t      - MLP\n914\t      - Graded, L2norm preferred\n915\t      - ✓\n916\t      - '~'\n917\t      - ✗(random preferred)\n918\t      - '~'\n919\t      - 2/4\n920\t    - - π0\n921\t      - Linear proj\n922\t      - Immune\n923\t      - ✓(offline)\n924\t      - —\n925\t      - —\n926\t      - —\n927\t      - 1/1\n928\t    notes: Total 11/17 ≈ 65%。π0.5 是 framework 最大 failure point。\n929\t  - title: 'Table L: Claim Survival Assessment'\n930\t    columns:\n931\t    - Claim\n932\t    - Original Status\n933\t    - Worst-Tier Status\n934\t    - Surviving Evidence\n935\t    rows:\n936\t    - - 'C1: 2-Axis Framework'\n937\t      - Primary contribution\n938\t      - Fails as theory\n939\t      - Descriptive taxonomy for L2norm-Object only\n940\t    - - 'C2: Pixel-Shuffle Entanglement'\n941\t      - Strong\n942\t      - Survives\n943\t      - Universal 0% across 4 suites × 2 methods\n944\t    - - 'C3: Connector-Specific Patterns'\n945\t      - Strong\n946\t      - Partial survival\n947\t      - MLP graded confirmed; linear 'immune' falsified\n948\t    - - 'C4: VTR Recovery'\n949\t      - Strong\n950\t      - Survives as case study\n951\t      - 0%→59% on SmolVLA; fails on OpenVLA\n952\t    - - 'C5: CV Scaling Law'\n953\t      - Novel contribution\n954\t      - Fails as universal\n955\t      - Within-Object heuristic only; cross-suite |ρ|≈0.45\n956\t    notes: 2-3 claims survive review intact. Paper viable as empirical study, not\n957\t      as theory paper.\n958\t  figures_description:\n959\t  - 'Fig framework accuracy heatmap: 5 models × 4 suites grid, color = (prediction\n960\t    correct / partially correct / wrong). Visual impact: scattered errors, no clean\n961\t    pattern.'\n962\t  - 'Fig revised paper narrative flow: from ''discover governing principle'' to ''provide\n963\t    systematic benchmark + catalog surprising findings''.'\n964\t  analysis: '在 worst 档，paper 的 identity 发生根本转变： FROM: \"We discover a principled 2-axis\n965\t    framework governing VLA token compressibility\" TO: \"We provide the first systematic\n966\t    study of token pruning across VLA architectures, revealing that pruning behavior\n967\t    is an irreducible function of (connector, method, k, task), not reducible to simple\n968\t    architectural rules\"\n969\t\n970\t    Key novel findings that survive independently of the framework: (1) Pixel-shuffle\n971\t    entanglement is real and irreversible — this is a genuine architectural insight\n972\t    (2) Importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture — supported\n973\t    by E5 attention data + π0.5 method divergence (3) L2norm is actively harmful on\n974\t    low-CV models — 36pp gap on π0.5, 28pp on X-VLA at k=0.5 Object (4) VTR achieves\n975\t    near-lossless compression for pixel-shuffle — 0%→59% at any M ratio\n976\t\n977\t    These 4 findings are individually publishable observations that together constitute\n978\t    a substantial empirical contribution for CoRL, even without a unified theory.\n979\t    Title: \"A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures.\"'\n980\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b17614-1ae9-46bc-87bd-87205f677c45","uuid":"c984cbca-7dc2-4002-97bc-9ee9874ae4f8","timestamp":"2026-05-25T06:17:35.631Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260525T050917/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '核心 reframe：从 ''principled 2-axis framework'' 转为 ''comprehensive\n  empirical study of VLA token pruning across architectures and tasks''。 π0.5 cross-suite\n  数据摧毁了两轴独立性假设——random k=0.9 在 Object=9% vs Goal=62.2%，同一 token-independent connector\n  跨 suite 差异达 53pp。 E5 attention pruning 数据（X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2% vs L2norm=42.6%）证明\n  ''entanglement'' 不是 connector 的固有属性，而是 importance metric 选择的 artifact。 CV scaling\n  law 仅在 Object suite 内部成立（Spearman ρ=-1.0），跨 suite 后 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm\n  > random），平均 |ρ|≈0.45。 VTR 确认为 SmolVLA-specific 方案（OpenVLA VTC-only 全部失败），且 M=96\n  dip (p=0.034) 暗示训练不稳定。 Title 改为 ''A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies\n  Across VLA Architectures''。 仍然 submit CoRL，因为 5 models × 4 suites × systematic comparison\n  是 substantial empirical contribution。 Claims 缩减为：(1) pixel-shuffle entanglement\n  是真实的架构属性（C2 survives），(2) importance metric 选择 > connector architecture（new empirical\n  finding），(3) VTR 在 pixel-shuffle 上实现 near-lossless compression（C4 survives as case\n  study）。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: 'Cross-Suite Expansion: π0.5 + X-VLA + OpenVLA + SmolVLA × 4 Suites'\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n  description: '将所有 5 models 的 pruning 实验从 Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。 核心目的：验证 2-axis\n    framework 的 cross-suite 一致性。 实际结果：framework 在 Object suite 上准确，但 cross-suite 后出现系统性偏差。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct: 9.3\n    pi05_random_k09_goal_sr_pct: 62.2\n    pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 54.0\n    pi05_random_k09_long_sr_pct: 31.4\n    pi05_random_k09_cross_suite_range_pp: 52.9\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct: 89.6\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 95.3\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct: 80.0\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_cross_suite_range_pp: 18.2\n    xvla_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 97.6\n    xvla_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct: 70.2\n    xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct: 78.8\n    xvla_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct: 27.5\n    xvla_l2norm_k095_long_sr_pct: 47.0\n    smolvla_k095_all_suites_sr_pct: <0.1 (all 4 suites)\n    cv_strategy_spearman_object: -1.0\n    cv_strategy_spearman_goal: -0.5\n    cv_strategy_spearman_long: 0.5\n    cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean: 0.45\n    delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_object_pp: 36.0\n    delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_goal_pp: 13.8\n    delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_long_pp: -4.6\n    delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_object_pp: 28.0\n    delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_goal_pp: 8.5\n    delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_long_pp: 17.0\n    delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_object_pp: -1.8\n    delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_goal_pp: 8.8\n    framework_accuracy_pct: 62\n    axis2_amplification_entangling_minus_independent_pp: 11.4\n    e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_object_sr_pct: 99.2\n    e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_goal_sr_pct: 98.2\n    e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial_sr_pct: 88.8\n    e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_long_sr_pct: 90.2\n    e5_xvla_attn_mean_k05_long_sr_pct: 94.0\n  result_rationale: 'π0.5 random k=0.9 在 Object 上出现 catastrophic cliff（9.3%），但在 Goal\n    上仅下降至 62.2%——同一 linear projection connector、同一 random method、同一 k，仅 task distribution\n    不同就产生 53pp 差异。这直接破坏 \"token-independent connector 不受 task complexity 影响\" 的核心假设。\n    机制：Object suite 需要 precise object identity discrimination（visually similar condiments），random\n    在 cliff zone 摧毁 concentrated discriminative features；Goal suite 的 task 由 language\n    instruction 区分，vision tokens 冗余度更高，random 破坏的影响小。 L2norm 在相同 k=0.9 的 cross-suite\n    range 仅 18.2pp（vs random 53pp），证明 cross-suite sensitivity 是 METHOD-dependent 而非\n    connector-dependent。 E5 attention pruning 数据更具破坏性：X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2%（Object）、98.2%（Goal），vs\n    L2norm=42.6%/59%。这意味着 X-VLA 的 \"entanglement\" 问题完全可以通过更换 importance metric 解决，BART\n    encoder 产生的不是 \"irreversible entanglement\" 而是 \"norm-unfriendly importance distribution\"。\n    CV scaling law 在 Object 内仍然成立（Spearman -1.0），但 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm >\n    random，Δ=-4.6pp），导致 cross-suite 平均 |ρ|≈0.45，远低于 paper 声称的 \"universal predictor\"\n    所需的 >0.8。 OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也出现 method preference reversal（random > L2norm +8.8pp），而\n    Object 上 L2norm > random（+1.8pp）。同一 CV=0.215 的 model，跨 suite 后 method preference\n    反转。 Framework 在 20 个 model×suite 预测中仅正确约 12 个（62%），达不到 \"principled framework\"\n    标准。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table A: Cross-Suite Δ(Random-L2norm) at k=0.5 — CV Scaling Law Breakdown'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - CV\n    - Object Δ(pp)\n    - Spatial Δ(pp)\n    - Goal Δ(pp)\n    - Long Δ(pp)\n    - Range(pp)\n    rows:\n    - - π0.5\n      - '0.055'\n      - '+36.0'\n      - '+16.0'\n      - '+13.8'\n      - '-4.6'\n      - '40.6'\n    - - X-VLA\n      - '0.151'\n      - '+28.0'\n      - '+12.6'\n      - '+8.5'\n      - '+17.0'\n      - '19.5'\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - '0.215'\n      - '-1.8'\n      - ~+5\n      - '+8.8'\n      - ~+3\n      - ~10.6\n    notes: Object suite 上 monotonic（ρ=-1.0），Long suite 上 π0.5 reversal 破坏 monotonicity。Cross-suite\n      mean |ρ|≈0.45。\n  - title: 'Table B: π0.5 Random k=0.9 Cross-Suite — Token-Independent ≠ Task-Independent'\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - Baseline(%)\n    - Random k=0.9(%)\n    - Δ from baseline(pp)\n    - L2norm k=0.9(%)\n    - Method gap(pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Object\n      - '98.2'\n      - '9.3'\n      - '-88.9'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '-88.9'\n    - - Spatial\n      - '97.2'\n      - '54.0'\n      - '-43.2'\n      - '95.3'\n      - '-41.3'\n    - - Goal\n      - '96.4'\n      - '62.2'\n      - '-34.2'\n      - '89.6'\n      - '-27.4'\n    - - Long\n      - '92.8'\n      - '31.4'\n      - '-61.4'\n      - '80.0'\n      - '-12.8'\n    notes: Cross-suite range 53pp for random vs 18pp for L2norm。Task sensitivity 是\n      method-specific，非 architecture-level property。\n  - title: 'Table C: E5 Attention Pruning Demolishes Entanglement Narrative (X-VLA\n      k=0.5)'\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - L2norm(%)\n    - Random(%)\n    - Attn-Last(%)\n    - Attn-Mean(%)\n    - Best Attn vs L2norm(pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Object\n      - '42.6'\n      - '70.6'\n      - '99.2'\n      - '98.4'\n      - '+56.6'\n    - - Spatial\n      - '58.8'\n      - '71.4'\n      - '88.8'\n      - '91.6'\n      - '+32.8'\n    - - Goal\n      - '59.0'\n      - '67.2'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '97.4'\n      - '+38.4'\n    - - Long\n      - '44.6'\n      - '61.6'\n      - '90.2'\n      - '94.0'\n      - '+49.4'\n    notes: Attention pruning 在所有 4 suites 上实现 88-99% SR at k=0.5。问题不在 connector entanglement，在\n      importance metric。\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig cross-suite heatmap: 5 models × 4 suites × 2 methods (L2norm/random) at k=0.5/k=0.9,\n    颜色编码 SR。清晰展示 framework 预测（虚线框）vs 实际结果的 mismatch areas。'\n  - 'Fig CV vs Δ(R-L2) scatter: 4 panels (one per suite), 每个 panel 3 个点 (π0.5/X-VLA/OpenVLA)，展示\n    scaling law 在 Object 上线性但在 Long 上崩溃。'\n  analysis: 'Cross-suite 数据系统性地破坏 2-axis framework 的两个核心预测： (1) Axis-1 独立性：token-independent\n    connectors should be immune to task complexity → π0.5 random k=0.9 Object=9% vs\n    Goal=62% 证伪（53pp gap）。 (2) CV universal predictor：CV 应在所有 suite 上预测 method preference\n    → Long-horizon 上 π0.5 出现 reversal（L2norm > random），OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也 reversal。\n    E5 attention pruning 数据进一步瓦解 Axis-1 定义：X-VLA（\"entangling\"）在 attention pruning\n    下表现如同 \"independent\" connector。Axis-1 的区分不在 \"token coupling\" 而在 \"susceptibility\n    to norm-based importance bias\"。 Reframe：论文不能声称发现了 governing principle，而应定位为 \"comprehensive\n    empirical study revealing that importance metric selection matters more than connector\n    architecture\"。\n\n    '\n- name: π0.5 Token-Independent Confirmation (4B, Linear Proj)\n  plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\n  description: 'π0.5 作为 2nd token-independent data point，验证 CV=0.055 的 linear projection\n    在所有 suite 上的 pruning 行为。 worst 档：π0.5 数据揭示 \"immune class\" 不存在——random pruning\n    在 cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) 产生 catastrophic collapse，且行为极度 task-dependent。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pi05_cv: 0.055\n    pi05_baseline_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n    pi05_baseline_spatial_sr_pct: 97.2\n    pi05_baseline_goal_sr_pct: 96.4\n    pi05_baseline_long_sr_pct: 92.8\n    pi05_random_k095_object_sr_pct: 71.1\n    pi05_random_k0925_object_sr_pct: 27.6\n    pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct: 10.8\n    pi05_random_k085_object_sr_pct: 5.0\n    pi05_random_k07_object_sr_pct: 75.5\n    pi05_random_k05_object_sr_pct: 69.4\n    pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct: 98.2\n    pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr_pct: 98.0\n    pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr_pct: 33.4\n    pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr_pct: 51.0\n    pi05_random_cliff_depth_pp: 66.1\n    pi05_l2norm_v_shape_depth_pp: 17.6\n    pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_cross_suite_avg_pp: 15.3\n    pi05_attention_k07_object_sr_pct: 0.6\n    pi05_attention_k05_object_sr_pct: 37.8\n    pi05_attention_k095_object_sr_pct: 98.4\n  result_rationale: 'π0.5（CV=0.055）本应是 \"immune\" class 的完美验证，但数据揭示了截然不同的图景： (1) Random-specific\n    cliff：k=0.95→71.1% → k=0.925→27.6% → k=0.9→10.8% → k=0.85→5.0%，在 10% keep ratio\n    变化范围内产生 66pp collapse。这个 cliff 是 random-specific 的——L2norm 在同区间保持 98.0-99.2% 的\n    plateau。 (2) Fixed-mask experiment 排除了 temporal inconsistency（T0=12% = per-call\n    12%），证明 cliff 是 spatial coverage 的 structural failure。 (3) V-shape non-monotonicity：L2norm\n    在 k=0.5 出现 valley（33.4%），k=0.7=55.0% 和 k=0.3=51.0% 都更高。Token position visualization\n    确认 k=0.5 恰好是 spatial clustering 最严重的点（1 cluster, 78% coverage）。 (4) Cross-suite\n    数据摧毁 \"immune\" 标签：random k=0.9 在 Object=9% 但 Goal=62.2%（+53pp），Spatial=54%，Long=31.4%。Object\n    的 concentrated critical features（visually similar condiments）在 cliff zone 极度脆弱，而\n    Goal 的 language-disambiguated tasks 对 random token loss 更 robust。 (5) Attention\n    pruning 不解决问题：k=0.7 attn=0.6%（比 random 的 75.5% 差 75pp），k=0.5 attn=37.8%（与 L2norm\n    33.4% 持平）。π0.5 的 attention map 不提供有效 importance signal。 In worst tier, π0.5 从\n    \"immune class exemplar\" 降级为 \"case study demonstrating that pruning behavior is\n    an irreducible function of method × k × task, not a simple connector property\"。Cross-suite\n    average Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5 = (+36+16+13.8-4.6)/4 = 15.3pp，远低于 Object-only 的 36pp。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table D: π0.5 Random Cliff Zone (Object Suite)'\n    columns:\n    - k\n    - Tokens kept\n    - Random SR(%)\n    - L2norm SR(%)\n    - Δ(L2-R)(pp)\n    rows:\n    - - '0.95'\n      - '730'\n      - '71.1'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '+27.1'\n    - - '0.925'\n      - '710'\n      - '27.6'\n      - '99.2'\n      - '+71.6'\n    - - '0.90'\n      - '691'\n      - '10.8'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '+87.4'\n    - - '0.85'\n      - '653'\n      - '5.0'\n      - '98.0'\n      - '+93.0'\n    - - '0.70'\n      - '538'\n      - '75.5'\n      - '55.0'\n      - '-20.5'\n    - - '0.50'\n      - '384'\n      - '69.4'\n      - '33.4'\n      - '-36.0'\n    - - '0.30'\n      - '230'\n      - '36.4'\n      - '51.0'\n      - '+14.6'\n    notes: 方法偏好在 k=0.7 附近反转。Cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) L2norm 完胜；aggressive zone (k=0.5-0.7)\n      random 完胜。\n  - title: 'Table E: π0.5 Cross-Suite Random k=0.9 — ''Immune'' Class Falsified'\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - Baseline(%)\n    - Random k=0.9(%)\n    - L2norm k=0.9(%)\n    - Δ from baseline (random, pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Object\n      - '98.2'\n      - '9.3'\n      - '98.2'\n      - '-88.9'\n    - - Spatial\n      - '97.2'\n      - '54.0'\n      - '95.3'\n      - '-43.2'\n    - - Goal\n      - '96.4'\n      - '62.2'\n      - '89.6'\n      - '-34.2'\n    - - Long\n      - '92.8'\n      - '31.4'\n      - '80.0'\n      - '-61.4'\n    notes: 同一 model/method/k，cross-suite range=53pp。Framework 预测 token-independent\n      应 <5pp variation。\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig π0.5 dual-method pruning curve: x=k, y=SR, two lines (random/L2norm), Object\n    suite。突出 random cliff zone 和 L2norm V-shape valley。'\n  - 'Fig π0.5 4-suite comparison: 4 panels, 每 panel 一个 suite, random+L2norm curves。展示\n    cross-suite behavior divergence。'\n  analysis: 'π0.5 数据是 worst 档的 smoking gun：CV=0.055 的 pure linear projection 不 \"immune\"，只是\n    L2norm 恰好在 cliff zone 有效。 换用 random pruning，即出现 catastrophic cliff。换 suite（Goal/Long），random\n    的 cliff 消失但 L2norm 的 advantage 也缩小。 这意味着 \"compressibility\" 不是 connector 的 intrinsic\n    property，而是 (connector, method, k, task) 四元组的 emergent property。 2-axis framework\n    的简化——将其压缩为 (connector, task) 二维——在 worst 档数据下失效。 Paper 需要 reframe：不是 \"connector\n    determines compressibility\"，而是 \"we provide the first comprehensive map of the\n    4D pruning landscape across VLA architectures\"。\n\n    '\n- name: VTR Cross-Suite Generalization (SmolVLA M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr\n  description: 'SmolVLA VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long suites 上的压缩性能验证。 worst 档：VTR\n    cross-suite recovery 衰减，且 VTR 训练在非 Object suite 上有不稳定性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    vtr_m32_object_sr_pct: 60.1\n    vtr_m32_spatial_sr_pct: 53.2\n    vtr_m32_goal_sr_pct: 56.4\n    vtr_m32_long_sr_pct_predicted: 48.0\n    smolvla_baseline_object_sr_pct: 59.2\n    smolvla_baseline_spatial_sr_pct: 44.6\n    smolvla_baseline_goal_sr_pct: 60.8\n    smolvla_baseline_long_sr_pct: 36.6\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_object: 1.015\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial: 1.193\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_goal: 0.928\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_long_predicted: 0.874\n    vtr_recovery_ratio_mean: 0.95\n    vtr_m96_dip_p_value: 0.034\n    vtr_m96_dip_confirmed: true\n    hard_pruning_k05_all_suites_sr_pct: 0.0\n  result_rationale: 'VTR M=32 在 Object 上实现 near-lossless compression（60.1% vs baseline\n    59.2%），Spatial 上甚至超过 baseline（53.2% vs 44.6%，可能因为 VTR 训练 regularization 效应）。 但\n    Goal suite recovery ratio = 56.4/60.8 = 0.928，低于 Object。预测 Long-horizon（未测）recovery\n    ratio 进一步下降至 ~0.87：Long tasks 需要 multi-step reasoning，VTR 的 cross-attention 可能无法完全保留\n    temporal action sequence 所需的 spatial information chain。 M=96 dip（p=0.034 vs M=64）在\n    worst 档被确认为 training instability（非 statistical fluke），因为 M=96 的 3-seed std=3.2pp\n    是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 VTR 的 flat M-curve 可能是 M=16-64 的幸运区间，M=96 暴露了 cross-attention\n    query 数量与 pixel-shuffle token structure 之间的 resonance 问题。 VTR 仍然是 valid contribution（从\n    0% hard pruning 恢复到 ~baseline），但 worst 档将其定位为 \"SmolVLA-specific case study\" 而非\n    \"general method\"，因为： (1) cross-suite recovery 有衰减（Goal 0.93, Long predicted 0.87），\n    (2) M=96 dip 暗示 training sensitivity， (3) OpenVLA VTR 完全失败（下条）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table F: VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery (SmolVLA)'\n    columns:\n    - Suite\n    - Hard Prune k=0.5(%)\n    - VTR M=32(%)\n    - Baseline(%)\n    - Recovery Ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Object\n      - '0.0'\n      - '60.1'\n      - '59.2'\n      - '1.015'\n    - - Spatial\n      - '0.6'\n      - '53.2'\n      - '44.6'\n      - '1.193'\n    - - Goal\n      - '0.0'\n      - '56.4'\n      - '60.8'\n      - '0.928'\n    - - Long (pred)\n      - '0.0'\n      - ~48\n      - '36.6'\n      - ~0.87\n    notes: Recovery ratio 从 Object(1.0) 下降到 Long(0.87)。VTR 在 complex tasks 上 recovery\n      衰减 ~13%。\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig VTR M-curve with error bars: x=M, y=SR, 3-seed error bars。M=96 dip 突出标注 p=0.034。'\n  - 'Fig VTR cross-suite bar chart: 4 suites × (hard prune / VTR M=32 / baseline)，展示\n    recovery gap 在 Long 上最大。'\n  analysis: 'VTR 从 \"universal compression method\" 降级为 \"effective recovery tool for\n    pixel-shuffle connectors, with decreasing efficacy on complex tasks\"。 M=96 dip\n    的 statistical significance (p=0.034) 不足以证明 systematic failure（n=3 power ~0.2），但足以引起\n    reviewer 对 training stability 的质疑。 Cross-suite recovery 衰减是合理的：VTR 在 Object suite\n    上训练，cross-suite 是 zero-shot transfer。Long-horizon tasks 的 action sequence 依赖 precise\n    temporal-spatial correspondence，VTR 的 cross-attention bottleneck 可能丢失这些 long-range\n    dependencies。 Paper 策略：VTR 作为 §4.7 的 case study 保留，但移除 \"universal compression\"\n    措辞，改为 \"recovers pixel-shuffle cliff-edge to near-baseline on trained distribution,\n    with ~13% degradation on out-of-distribution complex tasks\"。\n\n    '\n- name: 'VTR Universality Test: OpenVLA MLP Projector (M=128/32/64)'\n  plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\n  description: 'VTR 在 OpenVLA（MLP projector）上的泛化性测试。M=128 full VTR 已失败（0% SR），VTC-only\n    M=32/M=64 作为 fallback。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    openvla_vtr_m128_sr_pct: 0.0\n    openvla_vtconly_m32_sr_pct_predicted: 3.0\n    openvla_vtconly_m64_sr_pct_predicted: 5.0\n    openvla_vtconly_m96_sr_pct_predicted: 2.0\n    openvla_baseline_sr_pct: 74.0\n    overfitting_confirmed: true\n    failure_mode: model outputs identical action every timestep\n  result_rationale: 'M=128 VTR 在 20K steps 后 0% SR（model 对所有 observation 输出相同 action）确认\n    severe overfitting。 VTC-only M=32/M=64 预测同样失败（<5% SR），因为根本原因不在 VTR architecture\n    而在 MLP projector tokens 的特性： (1) MLP projector tokens 已经是 individually meaningful\n    的（CV=0.215, 有 gradient differentiation），VTR 的 cross-attention 无法提供额外信息，反而引入 information\n    bottleneck。 (2) OpenVLA 的 256 tokens × 7B parameters 的 scale 与 SmolVLA 的 128 tokens\n    × 450M parameters 完全不同——VTR 的 ~22M params 对 7B model 来说是 rounding error，无法学到有意义的\n    re-encoding。 (3) M=96/M=64/M=32 的 training loss 持续下降但 eval SR 不恢复，典型的 action space\n    overfitting pattern。 在 worst 档，这确认 VTR 是 pixel-shuffle-specific method。Paper 中\n    VTR 需要 reframe：不是 \"universal compression tool\" 而是 \"architecture-specific recovery\n    mechanism that works because pixel-shuffle tokens need re-entangling, while MLP\n    tokens are already independent and don''t benefit from cross-attention re-encoding\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table G: VTR on OpenVLA — Universal Failure'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - M\n    - Params(M)\n    - Steps\n    - Train Loss\n    - SR(%)\n    rows:\n    - - Full VTR\n      - '128'\n      - '22.2'\n      - 20K\n      - converged\n      - '0.0'\n    - - VTC-only\n      - '32'\n      - '22.2'\n      - 100K\n      - converged\n      - ~3\n    - - VTC-only\n      - '64'\n      - '22.2'\n      - 100K\n      - converged\n      - ~5\n    - - VTC-only\n      - '96'\n      - '22.2'\n      - 100K\n      - converged\n      - ~2\n    - - LoRA baseline\n      - —\n      - '883'\n      - 100K\n      - '0.065'\n      - '0.0'\n    notes: '所有 VTR configs 失败。Train loss 收敛但 SR ≈0。Failure mode: identical action\n      output。'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig overfitting diagnostic: training loss curve (converging) + eval SR curve\n    (flat at 0%), 展示 train/eval disconnect。'\n  analysis: 'VTR universality 完全失败。这不是 hyperparameter tuning 问题——M=128/96/64/32 全部\n    <5% SR，且 LoRA fine-tuning 也产生 0% SR（libero_lora_baseline），说明 OpenVLA 的 fine-tuning\n    本身就 fragile。 Reviewer 会问：\"如果 VTR 只在 SmolVLA 上 work，它是在修复 pixel-shuffle entanglement\n    还是只是在 SmolVLA 的特定 action space 上 overfit？\" Response 策略：M=128 passthrough control（58.0%\n    ≈ baseline 59.2%）证明 VTR 确实在学 re-encoding 而非 action space memorization。但这个 argument\n    仅对 SmolVLA 成立。\n\n    '\n- name: OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96)\n  plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep\n  description: 'OpenVLA 上的 VTC cross-attention compressor M-sweep。所有 M 值预期失败。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    openvla_vtc_m32_sr_pct: 0.0\n    openvla_vtc_m64_sr_pct: 0.0\n    openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss: 2.45\n    openvla_vtc_m96_sr_pct: 0.0\n    all_m_values_fail: true\n  result_rationale: 'M=96 已训完（final train loss 2.45, eval loss 2.66），远高于 SmolVLA VTR\n    的 ~0.05 train loss。这不是欠拟合——100K steps with OpenVLA 的 tokenized action space 天然产生高\n    cross-entropy loss。 M=32/M=64 的 v3/v4/v5 版本反复失败（disk full, GPU crash, training\n    instability），即使成功训完也预期 0% SR。 根本原因：OpenVLA 使用 discrete tokenized actions（不是 continuous\n    actions），VTC 的 cross-attention 将 256 个 vision tokens 压缩到 M 个 queries，但 OpenVLA\n    的 LLM decoder 期望完整的 256-token vision context 来做 autoregressive action token generation。压缩后的\n    M queries 无法提供 decoder 所需的 token-level spatial precision。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '确认 VTR/VTC 在 MLP projector + discrete action space 的组合下无效。 Paper 中作为\n    negative result 报告：VTR effectiveness = f(connector_type)，strengthens architecture-dependency\n    narrative。\n\n    '\n- name: X-VLA Cliff Threshold Localization (k=0.80/0.85, 3-seed)\n  plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization\n  description: 'X-VLA 在 k=0.80 和 k=0.85 的 3-seed 精确定位 cliff。Non-monotonic pattern\n    已确认。 worst 档：cliff 是真实的，但 E5 attention pruning 证明它是 L2norm-specific artifact。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_mean: 89.0\n    xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_std: 0.72\n    xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_mean: 67.9\n    xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_std: 0.31\n    xvla_l2norm_nonmonotonic_gap_pp: 21.1\n    xvla_random_k085_sr_mean: 63.6\n    xvla_random_k080_sr_mean: 89.4\n    xvla_e5_attn_k05_sr_mean: 98.4\n    cliff_is_l2norm_specific: true\n    cliff_is_method_independent: false\n  result_rationale: 'X-VLA k=0.85 L2norm = 67.9%±0.31pp（3-seed，SD<1pp 确认完全 deterministic）。k=0.80\n    = 89.0%±0.72pp。 Non-monotonic gap = 21.1pp（k=0.85 < k=0.80），2-token 差异产生 21pp\n    SR change。Random pruning 在同区间也出现 cliff（63.6% vs 89.4%），但 per-task crash pattern\n    不同（T4, T6 both crash across methods → architectural bottleneck）。 在 worst 档，这个\n    cliff 的意义被 E5 attention pruning 完全重新诠释： - L2norm k=0.5 = 42.6% → attn_last k=0.5\n    = 99.2%（+56.6pp） - 同样的 50 tokens，同样的 k=0.5（保留 25 tokens），attention 几乎完美而 L2norm\n    catastrophic - 因此 cliff 不是 \"BART encoder entanglement creates irreversible token\n    dependencies\"，而是 \"L2norm 在 BART encoder 的 near-uniform norm distribution 上退化为\n    spatially clustered selection\" - Reviewer argument：\"如果换 importance metric 就消除了\n    cliff，那 Axis-1 的 ''token coupling'' 定义有根本缺陷——关键不在 coupling 而在 importance metric。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table H: X-VLA Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic'\n    columns:\n    - k\n    - L2norm SR(%)\n    - L2norm SD(pp)\n    - Random SR(%)\n    - Attn-Last SR(%)\n    rows:\n    - - '0.90'\n      - '97.6'\n      - —\n      - '97.8'\n      - ~99\n    - - '0.85'\n      - '67.9'\n      - '0.31'\n      - '63.6'\n      - ~97\n    - - '0.80'\n      - '89.0'\n      - '0.72'\n      - '89.4'\n      - ~99\n    - - '0.70'\n      - '56.2'\n      - —\n      - '65.2'\n      - '99.2'\n    - - '0.50'\n      - '42.6'\n      - —\n      - '70.6'\n      - '99.2'\n    notes: Attention pruning 完全消除 cliff 和 degradation。问题在 metric 不在 architecture。\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig X-VLA 3-method comparison: L2norm (cliff+degradation), Random (moderate degradation),\n    Attention (near-flat). 三条 curve 在同一 plot 上，清晰展示 metric choice 的 decisive role。'\n  analysis: 'Cliff localization 数据本身是 solid experimental result。但在 worst 档，E5 data\n    完全改变其解读： cliff 不是 connector architecture 的 intrinsic property，而是 L2norm importance\n    metric 在 low-CV distribution 上的 pathological behavior。 Attention pruning（zero\n    additional training）消除所有 degradation，这意味着 BART encoder 并没有 \"entangle\" tokens in\n    a way that prevents pruning，它只是让 tokens 的 L2-norm 不再是 good importance proxy。 Paper\n    需要重新定义 Axis-1：从 \"token coupling\" 改为 \"importance metric suitability\"，或者承认 2-axis\n    framework 是 L2norm-specific observation 而非 architecture-level insight。\n\n    '\n- name: OFT CV Diagnostic (Token Importance Measurement)\n  plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv\n  description: 'OpenVLA-OFT 的 token importance CV 测量。Expected CV≈0.219（≈Standard OpenVLA）。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    oft_cv: 0.219\n    oft_cv_std: 0.012\n    oft_entropy: 0.667\n    openvla_standard_cv: 0.215\n    cv_delta_pp: 0.4\n    sr_eval_blocked: true\n    gpu_incompatibility: Blackwell SDPA requires A100+torch2.2\n  result_rationale: 'OFT CV=0.219 ≈ Standard OpenVLA CV=0.215（Δ=0.004），确认 connector（3-layer\n    MLP）而非 action head（OFT vs standard）决定 token importance distribution。 Entropy 也几乎相同（0.667\n    vs 0.661）。这是 framework 的 positive confirmation——same connector → same CV → same\n    predicted pruning behavior。 但在 worst 档，这个 data point 的价值有限： (1) 无法在 LIBERO 上 eval\n    SR（Blackwell GPU SDPA 不兼容），所以 CV 预测没有 ground truth 验证 (2) OFT 和 Standard OpenVLA\n    用相同 connector 产生相同 CV 是 trivially expected，不提供 additional discrimination power\n    (3) Reviewer 会指出：\"你们有 6 个 model 的 CV，但只有 4 个能实际 eval SR。CV 作为 predictor 的 validation\n    set 太小。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table I: Diagnostic Metrics — 6-Model Spectrum'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Connector\n    - CV\n    - Entropy\n    - Eval SR Available?\n    rows:\n    - - π0\n      - Pure linear\n      - '0.038'\n      - '0.959'\n      - Offline only\n    - - π0.5\n      - Pure linear (×√d)\n      - '0.055'\n      - —\n      - Yes (4 suites)\n    - - X-VLA\n      - Linear + BART 12L\n      - '0.151'\n      - '0.614'\n      - Yes (4 suites)\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - 3-layer MLP\n      - '0.215'\n      - '0.661'\n      - Yes (Object only)\n    - - OFT\n      - 3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP)\n      - '0.219'\n      - '0.667'\n      - No (GPU blocked)\n    - - SmolVLA\n      - Pixel-shuffle\n      - '0.314'\n      - '0.952'\n      - Yes (4 suites)\n    notes: 6 models 有 CV，但仅 3 models 有 full cross-suite SR。OFT 和 π0 只有 diagnostic\n      metrics。\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'OFT CV 完成了 6-model diagnostic table，但不改变任何结论。在 worst 档，这是 incrementally\n    supportive 而非 decisive evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: OFT Full Graded-Class Evaluation (4 Suites)\n  plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full\n  description: 'OpenVLA-OFT 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 上的 baseline + pruning evaluation。\n    worst 档：GPU 不兼容问题持续，无法完成 evaluation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    eval_blocked: true\n    blocker: Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility with OpenVLA-OFT\n    workaround_attempted: A100 rental, torch2.2 downgrade — both failed\n    fallback_evidence: CV=0.219≈OpenVLA, entropy=0.667≈0.661 — inferred graded behavior\n    paper_impact: Missing 2nd graded-class SR data point, relies on CV inference\n    reviewer_risk: Moderate — 2/3 connector classes have ≥2 SR-evaluated models, MLP\n      class has only 1\n  result_rationale: 'OFT evaluation 在 worst 档仍然被 GPU 不兼容阻塞。Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA implementation\n    与 OFT checkpoint 的 torch 版本不兼容，降级 torch 或租用 A100 都不可行（timeline 限制）。 Paper 只能用\n    CV/entropy comparison 间接 argue OFT follows OpenVLA pattern。Reviewer 会注意到 MLP projector\n    class 只有 OpenVLA 1 个 model 有 SR data，不足以 generalize。 CogACT（literature baseline,\n    MLP projector, 74.8%→74.2% under 78% pruning from EfficientVLA）可以作为 external evidence，但不是\n    our own evaluation。 In worst tier, this is a clear gap but not fatal — pixel-shuffle\n    (SmolVLA, 1 model, universal 0%) and linear (π0/π0.5, 2 models, variable) are\n    well-characterized. MLP class has 1 internal + 1 external data point.\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Missing OFT SR data 在 worst 档是 acknowledged limitation。Reviewer concern\n    等级 \"moderate\"——不会 reject paper，但会要求 camera-ready 补充或更 cautious language about\n    MLP class generalization。\n\n    '\n- name: Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo) — 3rd Connector Family\n  plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\n  description: 'RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) 在 LIBERO 上 fine-tune\n    + pruning。 worst 档：fine-tuning 产生低 baseline，且 Perceiver 不清晰地落入 2-axis taxonomy。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    fine_tuning_baseline_sr_pct_predicted: 18.0\n    fine_tuning_difficulty: high — requires custom training pipeline adaptation\n    perceiver_cv_predicted: 0.28\n    perceiver_pruning_k09_predicted_sr_pct: 4.0\n    perceiver_pruning_k05_predicted_sr_pct: 0.0\n    taxonomy_fit: ambiguous — cross-attention creates partial entanglement different\n      from both pixel-shuffle and BART\n    paper_inclusion: dropped — insufficient time and unclear taxonomy value\n  result_rationale: 'RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档面临多重困难： (1) Fine-tuning infrastructure：RoboFlamingo\n    使用 Flamingo-style cross-attention perceiver resampler，将 variable-length vision\n    tokens 压缩到 fixed 64 queries。这需要 custom training pipeline，previous attempts (train_c5_roboflamingo_v2)\n    被 killed。 (2) Low baseline：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 在 LIBERO manipulation\n    tasks 上可能不如 direct projection（SmolVLA 59.2%, OpenVLA 74%），因为 LIBERO 需要 precise\n    spatial information 而 perceiver 天然是 lossy compression。预测 baseline ~18% SR。 (3)\n    Taxonomy ambiguity：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 与 BART encoder 的 self-attention\n    和 pixel-shuffle 的 spatial folding 都不同。它是 \"learned entanglement\" 而非 \"structural\n    entanglement\"。CV 可能在 0.2-0.3 range，不清晰地落入现有 taxonomy。 (4) Timeline：距 abstract\n    deadline 1 天，paper deadline 4 天，没有时间 debug fine-tuning pipeline + run full evaluation。\n    In worst tier, RoboFlamingo 被 dropped from paper。这减少了 paper 的 connector family\n    覆盖（3→2 confirmed families），但避免了 messy data 进一步复杂化已经 fragile 的 framework。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Dropping RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档是 rational choice：paper 已经有足够的 models（5\n    models × 4 suites）作为 empirical contribution，加入一个 low-baseline 的新 connector 只会模糊\n    narrative。 但这意味着 paper 的 connector 覆盖限于 linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle 三类，reviewer 可能指出\n    \"what about attention-based connectors (Perceiver, Q-Former)?\" 作为 limitation。\n\n    '\n- name: VTR M-Sweep Completion (SmolVLA 3-seed × 5 M-values)\n  plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\n  description: 'SmolVLA VTR M-sweep 的 3-seed 完成和 MLP adapter control。 worst 档：数据 solid\n    但 M=96 dip 和 high variance 引起质疑。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    m16_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 56.9\n    m16_3seed_std_pp: 1.3\n    m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 60.1\n    m32_3seed_std_pp: 1.3\n    m64_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 62.0\n    m64_3seed_std_pp: 2.3\n    m96_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 54.5\n    m96_3seed_std_pp: 3.2\n    m128_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 58.0\n    m128_3seed_std_pp: 3.5\n    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct: 63.4\n    mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std_pp: 2.6\n    vtc_vs_mlp_pvalue: 0.15\n    m64_vs_m96_pvalue: 0.034\n    baseline_sr_pct: 59.2\n    m_curve_flat_within_3pp: true\n    m96_dip_significant: true\n  result_rationale: 'VTR M-sweep 数据 intrinsically solid：M=16(56.9%) 到 M=128(58.0%)\n    都在 baseline 59.2% 的 ±5pp 内，证明 near-lossless compression at any ratio。MLP adapter\n    control（63.4%）与 VTC（60.1%）无显著差异（p=0.15），确认 architecture independence。 但 worst\n    档关注两个 weakness： (1) M=96 dip（54.5%, p=0.034 vs M=64=62.0%）虽然在 Bonferroni correction\n    后 marginally significant，但 3.2pp std 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 training instability——某些\n    seed/M 组合在 training dynamics 中进入 suboptimal basin。 (2) M=128 passthrough 的 3.5pp\n    std 也高，且 seed43=54.0% 是 outlier（其他两个 seed 59.8/60.2%）。如果 passthrough control 本身有\n    6pp variance，\"near-lossless\" 的声称需要 caveat。 In worst tier, VTR 仍然是 valid method（0%→~59%\n    recovery），但 training stability concern 使其从 \"recommended practice\" 降级为 \"promising\n    but needs further investigation\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table J: VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Results'\n    columns:\n    - M\n    - Compression(%)\n    - Mean SR(%)\n    - Std(pp)\n    - Individual Seeds\n    - vs Baseline\n    rows:\n    - - '16'\n      - '87.5'\n      - '56.9'\n      - '1.3'\n      - 55.8/58.4/56.5\n      - -2.3pp\n    - - '32'\n      - '75.0'\n      - '60.1'\n      - '1.3'\n      - 61.6/59.2/59.6\n      - +0.9pp\n    - - '64'\n      - '50.0'\n      - '62.0'\n      - '2.3'\n      - 61.6/60.0/64.4\n      - +2.8pp\n    - - '96'\n      - '25.0'\n      - '54.5'\n      - '3.2'\n      - 52.6/58.2/52.8\n      - -4.7pp\n    - - '128'\n      - '0.0'\n      - '58.0'\n      - '3.5'\n      - 59.8/54.0/60.2\n      - -1.2pp\n    - - MLP-32\n      - '75.0'\n      - '63.4'\n      - '2.6'\n      - 65.2/64.6/60.4\n      - +4.2pp\n    notes: M=96 dip p=0.034。M=128 seed43=54.0 outlier。Flat M-curve 成立但 variance 在高\n      M 处增大。\n  figures_description:\n  - Fig M-curve with 3-seed error bars and baseline band (59.2%±3pp shaded). M=96\n    dip 和 M=128 variance clearly visible。\n  analysis: 'VTR 在 worst 档仍是 paper 的 positive contribution：hard pruning 0% → VTR ~59%\n    ≈ baseline 是 dramatic recovery。 但 M=96 dip 和 high-M variance 需要 honest reporting。建议\n    paper 用 M=32 或 M=64 作为 recommended setting（stable seeds, good compression ratio），将\n    M=96 dip 作为 \"open question: why does M=96 underperform?\" 放入 discussion。 Reviewer\n    concern level: low-moderate. VTR 的 core claim（recovery from 0% to baseline）is\n    robust. M=96 是 interesting anomaly 但不 undermine main contribution。\n\n    '\n- name: Consolidated Cross-Suite Framework Accuracy Assessment\n  plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n  description: '综合所有 cross-suite 数据的 framework 准确率评估。 worst 档：framework accuracy ~62%，不足以支撑\n    \"principled framework\" 定位。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    framework_predictions_total: 20\n    framework_predictions_correct: 12\n    framework_accuracy_pct: 62\n    claims_surviving_review: 2.5\n    surviving_claims: C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement), C4 (VTR case study), partial\n      C3b (MLP graded)\n    failed_claims: C1 (2-axis framework as principled theory), C5 (CV universal predictor)\n    reframed_claims: C1→empirical observation catalog, C5→within-suite heuristic\n    paper_contribution_type: empirical study with surprising findings\n    corl_submission_viable: true\n    corl_acceptance_probability_pct: 45\n  result_rationale: 'Framework accuracy 计算方法： - SmolVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"catastrophic\n    at k=0.95\" → 实际 all suites ≤0.1% → 4/4 correct - X-VLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"entangling,\n    task-dependent collapse\" → Object OK (97.6%), Goal 70.2% (partial collapse), Spatial\n    78.8% (moderate), Long 27.5% (collapse) → 3/4 correct（Object 不 collapse，与预测不符）\n    - π0.5 × 4 suites: 预测 \"independent, immune to task complexity\" → Object random\n    k=0.9=9%（NOT immune!），但 L2norm=98.2% → method-dependent → 1/4 correct（框架不区分 method）\n    - OpenVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \"graded, L2norm preferred\" → Object L2norm>random (+1.8pp\n    ✓), Goal random>L2norm (+8.8pp ✗) → 2/4 correct - π0 × offline: 预测 \"immune\" →\n    k=0.1 improves → 1/1 correct Total: 4+3+1+2+1 = 11/17 = 65%（≈62% with margin of\n    error）\n\n    Claims survival analysis: - C1 (2-axis framework): FAILS as theory → survives\n    as \"descriptive taxonomy for L2norm pruning on Object suite\" - C2 (pixel-shuffle\n    entanglement): SURVIVES — universal 0% across all suites/methods/k is unambiguous\n    - C3a (linear proj depends on pipeline): Partially survives — π0 immune, π0.5\n    method-dependent, X-VLA cliff - C3b (MLP graded): Survives on Object — graded\n    curve confirmed - C4 (VTR): Survives as SmolVLA case study — 0%→59% recovery -\n    C5 (CV predicts strategy): FAILS as universal law → survives as \"within-Object-suite\n    heuristic\"\n\n    2.5 claims survive: C2, C4, half of C3b.\n\n    CoRL viability: paper 作为 \"comprehensive empirical study\" 仍然 viable（5 models ×\n    4 suites × 3 methods 是任何 VLA pruning 工作中最大规模的 comparison）。Acceptance probability\n    ~45%——足够好的 empirical contribution 但缺少 unified theory 会让某些 reviewers 觉得 \"incremental\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table K: Framework Prediction Accuracy by Model'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Connector Class\n    - Framework Prediction\n    - Object\n    - Spatial\n    - Goal\n    - Long\n    - Accuracy\n    rows:\n    - - SmolVLA\n      - Pixel-shuffle\n      - Catastrophic all suites\n      - ✓\n      - ✓\n      - ✓\n      - ✓\n      - 4/4\n    - - X-VLA\n      - BART encoder\n      - Task-dependent collapse\n      - ✗(no collapse)\n      - ✓\n      - ✓\n      - ✓\n      - 3/4\n    - - π0.5\n      - Linear proj\n      - Immune to task complexity\n      - ✗(random cliff)\n      - ✗\n      - ✗\n      - ✗\n      - 1/4\n    - - OpenVLA\n      - MLP\n      - Graded, L2norm preferred\n      - ✓\n      - '~'\n      - ✗(random preferred)\n      - '~'\n      - 2/4\n    - - π0\n      - Linear proj\n      - Immune\n      - ✓(offline)\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 1/1\n    notes: Total 11/17 ≈ 65%。π0.5 是 framework 最大 failure point。\n  - title: 'Table L: Claim Survival Assessment'\n    columns:\n    - Claim\n    - Original Status\n    - Worst-Tier Status\n    - Surviving Evidence\n    rows:\n    - - 'C1: 2-Axis Framework'\n      - Primary contribution\n      - Fails as theory\n      - Descriptive taxonomy for L2norm-Object only\n    - - 'C2: Pixel-Shuffle Entanglement'\n      - Strong\n      - Survives\n      - Universal 0% across 4 suites × 2 methods\n    - - 'C3: Connector-Specific Patterns'\n      - Strong\n      - Partial survival\n      - MLP graded confirmed; linear 'immune' falsified\n    - - 'C4: VTR Recovery'\n      - Strong\n      - Survives as case study\n      - 0%→59% on SmolVLA; fails on OpenVLA\n    - - 'C5: CV Scaling Law'\n      - Novel contribution\n      - Fails as universal\n      - Within-Object heuristic only; cross-suite |ρ|≈0.45\n    notes: 2-3 claims survive review intact. Paper viable as empirical study, not\n      as theory paper.\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig framework accuracy heatmap: 5 models × 4 suites grid, color = (prediction\n    correct / partially correct / wrong). Visual impact: scattered errors, no clean\n    pattern.'\n  - 'Fig revised paper narrative flow: from ''discover governing principle'' to ''provide\n    systematic benchmark + catalog surprising findings''.'\n  analysis: '在 worst 档，paper 的 identity 发生根本转变： FROM: \"We discover a principled 2-axis\n    framework governing VLA token compressibility\" TO: \"We provide the first systematic\n    study of token pruning across VLA architectures, revealing that pruning behavior\n    is an irreducible function of (connector, method, k, task), not reducible to simple\n    architectural rules\"\n\n    Key novel findings that survive independently of the framework: (1) Pixel-shuffle\n    entanglement is real and irreversible — this is a genuine architectural insight\n    (2) Importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture — supported\n    by E5 attention data + π0.5 method divergence (3) L2norm is actively harmful on\n    low-CV models — 36pp gap on π0.5, 28pp on X-VLA at k=0.5 Object (4) VTR achieves\n    near-lossless compression for pixel-shuffle — 0%→59% at any M ratio\n\n    These 4 findings are individually publishable observations that together constitute\n    a substantial empirical contribution for CoRL, even without a unified theory.\n    Title: \"A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures.\"'\n","numLines":980,"startLine":1,"totalLines":980}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015SBKZuqJ3mSv7K9URkiTXn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/\"},{\"title\":\"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, though the most detailed results are from CoRL 2023 and 2024. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL Review Criteria and Scoring\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Key Review Guidelines\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\n## Review Quality Standards\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and make reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nThe search results did not return the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer form or detailed scoring criteria scale. If you need the complete CoRL 2025 review form with specific scoring criteria, you may want to check the official CoRL 2025 website or OpenReview platform directly, as the most current information may not yet be fully indexed.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b17614-1ae9-46bc-87bd-87205f677c45","uuid":"88ad78ee-14e7-43ef-8e4b-f6cc806e4f5a","timestamp":"2026-05-25T06:17:37.862Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01WxLHhy969LXNc3YdUqxVRC","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/"},{"title":"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, though the most detailed results are from CoRL 2023 and 2024. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL Review Criteria and Scoring\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Key Review Guidelines\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\n## Review Quality Standards\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and make reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nThe search results did not return the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer form or detailed scoring criteria scale. If you need the complete CoRL 2025 review form with specific scoring criteria, you may want to check the official CoRL 2025 website or OpenReview platform directly, as the most current information may not yet be fully indexed."],"durationSeconds":6.101075709999999}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015khTy1a2xzHjyUNTfee6Dx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CoRL 2026 and review-related guidelines, though the specific 2026 reviewer guidelines review form was not directly available in these results. However, here's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Overview:**\nCoRL 2026 is an annual international conference focusing on the intersection of robotics and machine learning, and will be held in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**Related Resources:**\nThe search results show that OpenReview is being used as the platform for CoRL 2026 Conference. You can access the submission portal at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference.\n\nFor the specific reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026, I recommend checking the OpenReview platform directly or visiting the main CoRL 2026 website at corl.org, as the detailed reviewer guidelines document doesn't appear to be fully indexed in the current search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b17614-1ae9-46bc-87bd-87205f677c45","uuid":"c339f2f3-8e49-430d-b071-20f8d765b3d4","timestamp":"2026-05-25T06:17:42.224Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QPCwAAN9S3oamHK23Lygek","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about CoRL 2026 and review-related guidelines, though the specific 2026 reviewer guidelines review form was not directly available in these results. However, here's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Overview:**\nCoRL 2026 is an annual international conference focusing on the intersection of robotics and machine learning, and will be held in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**Related Resources:**\nThe search results show that OpenReview is being used as the platform for CoRL 2026 Conference. You can access the submission portal at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference.\n\nFor the specific reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026, I recommend checking the OpenReview platform directly or visiting the main CoRL 2026 website at corl.org, as the detailed reviewer guidelines document doesn't appear to be fully indexed in the current search results."],"durationSeconds":10.953957961000002}}
