{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W54iTN1e9NBS857Cm4oy6x","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale accept reject criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024 review instructions. Here's what the official CoRL 2024 instructions indicate:\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical. Results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Review Process\n\nACs will identify the desk rejection candidates, using one of the criteria below as a justification, and the PC will examine the candidates and make the final decision.\n\n## Author Feedback and Rebuttal\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period.\n\n## Transparency\n\nReviews and rebuttals of accepted papers will be made publicly available.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the specific numerical scoring scale (e.g., 1-10, 1-5, etc.) or detailed accept/reject thresholds that may be in the complete instructions for reviews document. The page content appears to be truncated. You may find more detailed scoring information by visiting the full CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b17614-1ae9-46bc-87bd-87205f677c45","uuid":"d18a7a92-2088-4e06-b359-7ea1a439ebbb","timestamp":"2026-05-25T06:17:54.084Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale accept reject criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014FHX7u5nUMDfJujrXRZH8p","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024 review instructions. Here's what the official CoRL 2024 instructions indicate:\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical. Results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Review Process\n\nACs will identify the desk rejection candidates, using one of the criteria below as a justification, and the PC will examine the candidates and make the final decision.\n\n## Author Feedback and Rebuttal\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period.\n\n## Transparency\n\nReviews and rebuttals of accepted papers will be made publicly available.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the specific numerical scoring scale (e.g., 1-10, 1-5, etc.) or detailed accept/reject thresholds that may be in the complete instructions for reviews document. The page content appears to be truncated. You may find more detailed scoring information by visiting the full CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews."],"durationSeconds":6.746854058000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TYEwkqqQhWWzUT78QeaFMm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric 1-10 scale review form questions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11000557/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"}]\n\nI found the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page. Let me search for more specific information about the scoring rubric and review form questions.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Configuring Review and Scoring Forms - Liaison International\",\"url\":\"https://help.liaisonedu.com/ResidencyCAS_Program_Help_Center/Program_Portal/Configuration/03_Review_and_Scoring_Forms\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Are numerical scores important for grant assessment? A cross-sectional study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11362741/\"},{\"title\":\"Is Peer Review Really in Decline? Analyzing Review Quality across Venues and Time\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.15172\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for the CoRL 2023 scoring rubric details.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 – Research Impact & Leadership\",\"url\":\"https://sites.gatech.edu/research/corl-2023/\"},{\"title\":\"Making better robots for humans: USC at CORL 2023 - USC Viterbi | School of Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://viterbischool.usc.edu/news/2023/11/making-better-robots-for-humans-usc-at-corl-2023/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Awards — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/awards\"}]\n\nLet me try searching for OpenReview CoRL 2023 to find the actual review form.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2023\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Workshop Deployable | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FWorkshop%2FDeployable\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Workshop L4SR | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FWorkshop%2FL4SR\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Workshop CRL WS | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FWorkshop%2FCRL_WS\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Workshop TGR | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FWorkshop%2FTGR\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference Submissions\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/submissions?venue=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2023/Conference\"},{\"title\":\"CoBeL-RL: A neuroscience-oriented simulation framework for complex behavior and learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2022.12.27.521997.full.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found information about the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines and Review Form\n\nThe review form begins with a \"Summary of Paper\" section that asks you to re-express the paper's position clearly and fairly, avoiding copy-and-paste from the paper's abstract and instead restating the contributions in your own words, which helps Area Chairs assess how others understand the paper's contributions.\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work, including questions about whether the problems or methods are new and whether the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques.\n\nUnder the Relevance criterion, reviewers are asked: Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method, or a learned model? Is the method evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both?\n\nWhile I found references to reviewer scores in the 3-5 range used at CoRL 2023, I was unable to locate the complete scoring rubric details with the specific 1-10 scale definitions or all review form questions from the official guidelines in my search results. For the most comprehensive and detailed information about the complete scoring rubric, review form questions, and their corresponding definitions, you may want to consult the full CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page directly at corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines or contact the conference organizers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b17614-1ae9-46bc-87bd-87205f677c45","uuid":"0b309573-40c5-4c40-ae5e-32a83833804a","timestamp":"2026-05-25T06:18:03.100Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric 1-10 scale review form questions","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_012XJdpburLZST8PJyri6Scu","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11000557/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/"},{"title":"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}]},"I found the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page. Let me search