{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WR4T6j44a2xj3anLEvLDoE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:corl2023.org reviewer guidelines quality significance originality scoring\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Statistical Reviewers Improve Reporting in Biomedical Articles: A Randomized Trial\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1824709/\"},{\"title\":\"Digital Scientific Platform for Independent Content in Neurology: Rigorous Quality Guideline Development and Implementation\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9227648/\"},{\"title\":\"Is Peer Review Really in Decline? Analyzing Review Quality across Venues and Time\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.15172\"},{\"title\":\"Peer Review of Grant Applications: Criteria Used and Qualitative Study of Reviewer Practices\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3460995/\"},{\"title\":\"Prior and Prejudice: The Novice Reviewers' Bias against Resubmissions in   Conference Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.14646\"},{\"title\":\"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"A Systematic Examination of Generative Artificial Intelligence (GAI) Usage Guidelines for Scholarly Publishing in Medical Journals\",\"url\":\"https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.03.19.24304550.full.pdf\"}]\n\nGreat! I found the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines. Here's what the document contains regarding reviewer evaluation criteria:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of this work. \n\nThe specific criteria are broken down as follows:\n\n**Originality:** The guidelines ask whether the problems or methods are new, whether it is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how the work differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n**Quality:** The assessment considers whether the submission is technically sound, whether claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, whether the methods used are appropriate, whether it is a complete piece of work or work in progress, and whether the authors are careful and honest about evaluating both strengths and weaknesses.\n\n**Clarity:** The guidelines assess whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\nThe document can be found at: https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b17614-1ae9-46bc-87bd-87205f677c45","uuid":"89f380a4-188f-4ada-b88d-7a241149a8e1","timestamp":"2026-05-25T06:18:13.004Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:corl2023.org reviewer guidelines quality significance originality scoring","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01K77BvbVwRDBqdf5j2LT2zV","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Statistical Reviewers Improve Reporting in Biomedical Articles: A Randomized Trial","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1824709/"},{"title":"Digital Scientific Platform for Independent Content in Neurology: Rigorous Quality Guideline Development and Implementation","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9227648/"},{"title":"Is Peer Review Really in Decline? Analyzing Review Quality across Venues and Time","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.15172"},{"title":"Peer Review of Grant Applications: Criteria Used and Qualitative Study of Reviewer Practices","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3460995/"},{"title":"Prior and Prejudice: The Novice Reviewers' Bias against Resubmissions in   Conference Peer Review","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.14646"},{"title":"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701"},{"title":"A Systematic Examination of Generative Artificial Intelligence (GAI) Usage Guidelines for Scholarly Publishing in Medical Journals","url":"https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.03.19.24304550.full.pdf"}]},"Great! I found the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines. Here's what the document contains regarding reviewer evaluation criteria:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of this work. \n\nThe specific criteria are broken down as follows:\n\n**Originality:** The guidelines ask whether the problems or methods are new, whether it is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how the work differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n**Quality:** The assessment considers whether the submission is technically sound, whether claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, whether the methods used are appropriate, whether it is a complete piece of work or work in progress, and whether the authors are careful and honest about evaluating both strengths and weaknesses.\n\n**Clarity:** The guidelines assess whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\nThe document can be found at: https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"],"durationSeconds":6.530198969999998}}
