{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TopRideSmkKy5abiv7uuyt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"已收集 CoRL 审稿标准。CoRL 评审维度：Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance (to robot learning), Limitations。接受率约 25-33%。评分使用 1-10 scale（OpenReview 标准）。\n\n现在并行派遣 R1（方法+实验）和 R2（新颖性+相关工作）进行独立盲审。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3605,"cache_read_input_tokens":64656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3605},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b17614-1ae9-46bc-87bd-87205f677c45","uuid":"5d9caafb-09be-458b-8cce-c78af6779941"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TopRideSmkKy5abiv7uuyt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LUSxDsPyqr6gx8jzrpSmku","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus is **methods and experiments**.\n\n## Venue: CoRL 2026\nCoRL is the Conference on Robot Learning. Acceptance rate ~25-33%. Review dimensions:\n- **Originality**: Are the problems/methods new? Novel combination of known techniques?\n- **Quality**: Technically sound? Claims well-supported by theory/experiments? Methods appropriate? Complete work vs work-in-progress?\n- **Clarity**: Well written, well organized?\n- **Significance**: Important results? Substantial contribution?\n- **Relevance**: Addresses robot learning? Evaluated on robots/simulation?\n- **Limitations**: Honestly reported?\n\nScoring scale (1-10): 1=strong reject, 3=clear reject, 5=marginally below, 6=marginally above, 7=good paper accept, 8=strong accept, 10=top 5%.\n\n## Your Role\nFocus on: experimental methodology, statistical rigor, evaluation protocol, reproducibility, ablation completeness, metric choice, claims vs evidence alignment.\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures\"\n\n**Core Claims**:\n1. Pixel-shuffle connectors (SmolVLA) create irreversible token entanglement — removing even 5% of tokens collapses SR to 0% across all 4 task suites and all pruning methods.\n2. Importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture — attention-based pruning achieves 99.2% SR on X-VLA at k=0.5 vs L2-norm's 42.6% (56.6pp gap).\n3. VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) achieves near-lossless compression for pixel-shuffle models (0%→~59%≈baseline at any compression ratio) but fails entirely on MLP-projector architectures (0% SR across all configs).\n\n**Models**: 5 VLA models (π0 3.3B, π0.5 4B, X-VLA 880M, OpenVLA 7B, SmolVLA 450M), spanning 3 connector families (linear projection, MLP, pixel-shuffle) + BART encoder variant.\n\n**Evaluation**: LIBERO benchmark, 4 task suites (Object, Spatial, Goal, Long-horizon), 500 episodes per condition (50 per task × 10 tasks). SR% as primary metric.\n\n**Key Tables and Data**:\n\nTable 1 (Diagnostic): 6-model CV spectrum from π0 (0.038) to SmolVLA (0.314). OFT CV=0.219 ≈ OpenVLA CV=0.215, but OFT has no SR eval (GPU blocked).\n\nTable 2 (π0.5 cross-suite random k=0.9): Object=9.3%, Spatial=54%, Goal=62.2%, Long=31.4%. L2norm: Object=98.2%, Spatial=95.3%, Goal=89.6%, Long=80%. Cross-suite range 53pp for random vs 18pp for L2norm.\n\nTable 3 (π0.5 cliff zone, Object): Random collapses from 71.1% (k=0.95) to 5.0% (k=0.85), while L2norm stays >98%. Method preference reverses at k≈0.7.\n\nTable 4 (X-VLA k=0.5 across metrics): L2norm=42.6-59%, Random=61.6-71.4%, Attn-Last=88.8-99.2%, Attn-Mean=91.6-98.4%. Best attn vs L2 gap: +32.8 to +56.6pp.\n\nTable 5 (X-VLA cliff, 3-seed): k=0.85 L2norm=67.9%±0.31pp, k=0.80=89.0%±0.72pp. Non-monotonic gap=21.1pp. Attention pruning eliminates all degradation.\n\nTable 6 (Cross-suite Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5): π0.5 Object=+36pp, Long=-4.6pp. Spearman ρ=-1.0 within Object, but cross-suite mean |ρ|≈0.45.\n\nTable 7 (VTR M-sweep, 3-seed): M=16→56.9%±1.3 to M=128→58.0%±3.5 (baseline=59.2%). M=96 dip to 54.5%±3.2 (p=0.034 vs M=64). MLP adapter control 63.4%±2.6.\n\nTable 8 (VTR cross-suite): Object recovery=1.015, Spatial=1.193, Goal=0.928, Long(pred)≈0.87.\n\nTable 9 (VTR on OpenVLA): All configs 0-5% SR despite converged training loss. LoRA baseline also 0%.\n\nTable 10 (Framework accuracy): SmolVLA 4/4, X-VLA 3/4, π0.5 1/4, OpenVLA 2/4, π0 1/1. Total ~62%.\n\nTable 11 (Claim survival): C1 fails as theory, C2 survives, C3 partial, C4 survives as case study, C5 fails as universal.\n\n**Experiment Design Reference** (what was planned but may not be fully reflected):\n- Cross-suite expansion planned for all 5 models × 4 suites — paper mostly covers this\n- VTR M-sweep with 3-seed stats — covered in paper  \n- VTR on OpenVLA (universality test) — covered (all fail)\n- X-VLA cliff localization with 3-seed — covered\n- OFT evaluation — blocked by GPU, only CV diagnostic available\n- Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo) — dropped from paper\n- OpenVLA VTC M-sweep — all fail, partially reported\n- VTR cross-suite generalization — covered but Long-horizon is predicted, not measured\n- E5 attention pruning on X-VLA — key data covered\n- Framework accuracy assessment — covered\n\n**Limitations acknowledged in paper**:\n1. Simulation only (LIBERO), no real robot\n2. MLP class: only OpenVLA has full SR eval (OFT blocked)\n3. Missing connector families: Perceiver, Q-Former\n4. Attention pruning only fully evaluated on X-VLA\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nWrite a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences, your own words)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted list, 4-6 items)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted list, 4-6 items, focus on methods/experiments)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (3-5 specific questions)\n5. **Missing Experiments / Ablations** (what would strengthen the paper)\n6. **Minor Issues** (formatting, typos, presentation)\n7. **Scores** (use CoRL 1-10 scale):\n   - Soundness (1-4 scale: 1=poor, 2=fair, 3=good, 4=excellent)\n   - Presentation (1-4)\n   - Contribution (1-4)\n   - Overall Score (1-10)\n   - Confidence (1-5: 1=low, 5=expert)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Point out both what works and what doesn't. Remember the venue is CoRL — robot learning relevance matters.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3605,"cache_read_input_tokens":64656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3605},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b17614-1ae9-46bc-87bd-87205f677c45","uuid":"0b4045a0-48d3-4e90-b1ba-b2660f7d4b40"}
